BESORAH.book({"id":"adam-eve-1","hebrew":"ADAM AND HAWWAH 1","english":"First Book of Adam and Eve","section":"Apocryphal","chapters":{"1":[[1,"On the third day, Aluahim planted the garden in the east of the earth, on the border of the world eastward, beyond which, towards the sun-rising, one finds nothing but water, that encompasses the whole world, and reaches to the borders of shamayim."],[2,"And to the north of the garden there is a sea of water, clear and pure to the taste, unlike anything else; so that, through the clearness thereof, one may look into the depths of the earth."],[3,"And when a man washes himself in it, he becomes clean of the cleanness thereof, and white of its whiteness - even if he were dark."],[4,"And Aluahim created that sea of his own good pleasure, for He knew what would come of the man He would make; so that after he had left the garden, on account of his transgression, men should be born in the earth. Among them are righteous ones who will die, whose nepheshoth Aluahim would raise at the last day; when all of them will return to their flesh, bathe in the water of that sea, and repent of their sins. 5 But when Aluahim made Adawm go out of the garden, He did not place him on the border of it northward. This was so that he and Ḥawwah would not be able to go near to the sea of water where they could wash themselves in it, be cleansed from their sins, erase the transgression they had committed, and be no longer reminded of it in the thought of their punishment."],[6,"As to the southern side of the garden, Aluahim did not want Adawm to live there either; because, when the ruach blew from the north, it would bring him, on that southern side, the delicious smell of the trees of the garden."],[7,"Wherefore Aluahim did not put Adawm there. This was so that he would not be able to smell the sweet smell of those trees, forget his transgression, and find consolation for what he had done by taking delight in the smell of the trees and yet not be cleansed from his transgression."],[8,"Again, also, because Aluahim is merciful and of great pity, and governs all things in a way that He alone knows - He made our father Adawm live in the western border of the garden, because on that side the earth is very broad."],[9,"And Aluahim commanded him to live there in a cave in a rock - the Cave of Treasures below the garden."]],"2":[[1,"But when our father Adawm, and Ḥawwah, went out of the garden, they walked the ground on their feet, not knowing they were walking."],[2,"And when they came to the opening of the gate of the garden, and saw the broad earth spread before them, covered with stones large and small, and with sand, they feared and trembled, and fell on their faces, from the fear that came over them; and they were as dead."],[3,"Because - whereas until this time they had been in the garden land, beautifully planted with all manner of trees - they now saw themselves, in a strange land, which they knew not, and had never seen."],[4,"And because, when they were in the garden they were filled with the chen of a bright nature, and they had not hearts turned toward earthly things."],[5,"Therefore Aluahim had pity on them; and when He saw them fallen before the gate of the garden, He sent His Word to our father, Adawm and Ḥawwah, and raised them from their fallen state."]],"3":[[1,"Aluahim said to Adawm, \"I have ordained on this earth days and years, and you and your descendants shall live and walk in them, until the days and years are fulfilled; when I shall send the Word that created you, and against which you have transgressed, the Word that made you come out of the garden, and that raised you when you were fallen."],[2,"Yes, the Word that will again save you when the five and a half days are fulfilled.\""],[3,"But when Adawm heard these words from Aluahim, and of the great five and a half days, he did not understand the meaning of them."],[4,"For Adawm was thinking there would be only five and a half days for him until the end of the world."],[5,"And Adawm cried, and prayed to Aluahim to explain it to him. 6 Then Aluahim in his mercy for Adawm who was made after His own image and likeness, explained to him, that these were 5,000 and"],[7,"But before that, Aluahim had made this berith with our father, Adawm, in the same terms, before he came out of the garden, when he was by the tree where Ḥawwah took of the fruit and gave it to him to eat."],[8,"Because, when our father Adawm came out of the garden, he passed by that tree, and saw how Aluahim had changed the appearance of it into another form, and how it shriveled."],[9,"And as Adawm went to it he feared, trembled and fell down; but Aluahim in His mercy lifted him up, and then made this berith with him."],[10,"And again, when Adawm was by the gate of the garden, and saw the cherub with a sword of flashing fire in his hand, and the cherub grew angry and frowned at him, both Adawm and Ḥawwah became afraid of him, and thought he meant to put them to death. So they fell on their faces, trembled with fear."],[11,"But he had pity on them, and showed them mercy; and turning from them went up to shamayim, and prayed to Yahuah, and said; -"],[12,"\"Yahuah, You sent me to watch at the gate of the garden, with a sword of fire."],[13,"But when Your servants, Adawm and Ḥawwah, saw me, they fell on their faces, and were as dead. O my Yahuah, what shall we do to Your servants?\""],[14,"Then Aluahim had pity on them, and showed them mercy, and sent His Mal'ak to keep the garden."],[15,"And the Word of Yahuah came to Adawm and Ḥawwah, and raised them up."],[16,"And Yahuah said to Adawm, \"I told you that at the end of the five and a half days, I will send my Word and save you."],[17,"Strengthen your heart, therefore, and stay in the Cave of Treasures, of which I have before spoken to you.\""],[18,"And when Adawm heard this Word from Aluahim, he was comforted with that which Aluahim had told him. For He had told him how He would save him."]],"4":[[1,"But Adawm and Ḥawwah cried for having come out of the garden, their first home."],[2,"And indeed, when Adawm looked at his flesh, that was altered, he cried bitterly, he and Ḥawwah, over what they had done. And they walked and went gently down into the Cave of Treasures."],[3,"And as they came to it, Adawm cried over himself and said to Ḥawwah, \"Look at this cave that is to be our prison in this world, and a place of punishment!"],[4,"What is it compared with the garden? What is its narrowness compared with the space of the other?"],[5,"What is this rock, by the side of those groves? What is the gloom of this cavern, compared with the light of the garden?"],[6,"What is this overhanging ledge of rock to shelter us, compared with the mercy of Yahuah that overshadowed us?"],[7,"What is the soil of this cave compared with the garden land? This earth, strewed with stones; and that, planted with delicious fruit trees?\""],[8,"And Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Look at your eyes, and at mine, which before beheld mal'akim praising in shamayim; and they too, without ceasing."],[9,"But now we do not see as we did; our eyes have become of flesh; they cannot see like they used to see before.\""],[10,"Adawm said again to Ḥawwah, \"What is our body today, compared to what it was in former days, when we lived in the garden?\""],[11,"After this, Adawm did not want to enter the cave, under the overhanging rock; nor would he ever want to enter it."],[12,"But he bowed to Aluahim's orders; and said to himself, \"Unless I enter the cave, I shall again be a transgressor.\""]],"5":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah entered the cave, and stood praying, in their own tongue, unknown to us, but which they knew well."],[2,"And as they prayed, Adawm raised his eyes and saw the rock and the roof of the cave that covered him overhead. This prevented him from seeing either shamayim or Aluahim's creatures. So he cried and beat his chest hard, until he dropped, and was as dead."],[3,"And Ḥawwah sat crying; for she believed he was dead."],[4,"Then she got up, spread her hands toward Aluahim, appealing to Him for mercy and pity, and said, \"O Aluahim, forgive me my sin, the sin which I committed, and don't remember it against me."],[5,"For I alone caused Your servant to fall from the garden into this condemned land; from light into this darkness; and from the house of joy into this prison."],[6,"O Aluahim, look at this Your servant fallen in this manner, and bring him back to life, that he may cry and repent of his transgression which he committed through me."],[7,"Don't take away his nephesh right now; but let him live that he may stand after the measure of his repentance, and do Your will, as before his death."],[8,"But if You do not bring him back to life, then, O Aluahim, take away my own nephesh, that I be like him, and leave me not in this dungeon, one and alone; for I could not stand alone in this world, but with him only."],[9,"For You, O Aluahim, caused him to fall asleep, and took a bone from his side, and restored the flesh in the place of it, by Your Mighty-like power."],[10,"And You took me, the bone, and make me a woman, bright like him, with heart, reason, and speech; and in flesh, like to his own; and You made me after the likeness of his looks, by Your mercy and power."],[11,"O Yahuah, I and he are one, and You, O Aluahim, are our Creator, You are He who made us both in one day."],[12,"Therefore, O Aluahim, give him life, that he may be with me in this strange land, while we live in it on account of our transgression."],[13,"But if You will not give him life, then take me, even me, like him; that we both may die the same day.\""],[14,"And Ḥawwah cried bitterly, and fell on our father Adawm; from her great sorrow."]],"6":[[1,"But Aluahim looked at them; for they had killed themselves through great grief. 2 But He decided to raise them and comfort them."],[3,"He, therefore, sent His Word to them; that they should stand and be raised immediately."],[4,"And Yahuah said to Adawm and Ḥawwah, \"You transgressed of your own free will, until you came out of the garden in which I had placed you."],[5,"Of your own free will have you transgressed through your desire for Aluahim, greatness, and an exalted state, such as I have; so that I deprived you of the bright nature in which you then were, and I made you come out of the garden to this land, rough and full of trouble."],[6,"If only you had not transgressed My mitsvah and had kept My law, and had not eaten of the fruit of the tree which I told you not to come near! And there were fruit trees in the garden better than that one."],[7,"But the wicked Satan did not keep his faith and had no good intent towards Me, that although I had created him, he considered Me to be useless, and sought the Aluahim for himself; for this I hurled him down from shamayim so that he could not remain in his first estate - it was he who made the tree appear pleasant in your eyes, until you ate of it, by believing his words."],[8,"Thus have you transgressed My mitsvah, and therefore I have brought on you all these sorrows."],[9,"For I am Aluahim the Creator, who, when I created My creatures, did not intend to destroy them. But after they had sorely roused My anger, I punished them with grievous plagues, until they repent."],[10,"But, if on the contrary, they still continue hardened in their transgression, they shall be under a curse forever.\""]],"7":[[1,"When Adawm and Ḥawwah heard these words from Aluahim, they cried and sobbed yet more; but they strengthened their hearts in Aluahim, because they now felt that Yahuah was to them like a father and a mother; and for this very reason, they cried before Him, and sought mercy from Him."],[2,"Then Aluahim had pity on them, and said: \"O Adawm, I have made My berith with you, and I will not turn from it; neither will I let you return to the garden, until My berith of the great five and a half days is fulfilled.\""],[3,"Then Adawm said to Aluahim, \"O Yahuah, You created us, and made us fit to be in the garden; and before I transgressed, You made all beasts come to me, that I should name them."],[4,"Your chen was then on me; and I named every one according to Your mind; and you made them all subject to me."],[5,"But now, O Yahuah Aluahim, that I have transgressed Your mitsvah, all beasts will rise against me and will devour me, and Ḥawwah Your handmaid; and will cut off our life from the face of the earth."],[6,"I therefore beg you, O Aluahim, that since You have made us come out of the garden, and have made us be in a strange land, You will not let the beasts hurt us.\""],[7,"When Yahuah heard these words from Adawm, He had pity on him, and felt that he had truly said that the beasts of the field would rise and devour him and Ḥawwah, because He, Yahuah, was angry with the two of them on account of their transgressions."],[8,"Then Aluahim commanded the beasts, and the birds, and all that moves on the earth, to come to Adawm and to be familiar with him, and not to trouble him and Ḥawwah; nor yet any of the good and righteous among their offspring."],[9,"Then all the beasts paid homage to Adawm, according to the mitsvah of Aluahim; except the serpent, against which Aluahim was angry. It did not come to Adawm, with the beasts."]],"8":[[1,"Then Adawm cried and said, \"O Aluahim, when we lived in the garden, and our hearts were lifted up, we saw the mal'akim that sang praises in shamayim, but now we can't see like we used to; no, when we entered the cave, all creation became hidden from us.\""],[2,"Then Aluahim Yahuah said to Adawm, \"When you were under subjection to Me, you had a bright nature within you, and for that reason could you see things far away. But after your transgression your bright nature was withdrawn from you; and it was not left to you to see things far away, but only near at hand; after the ability of the flesh; for it is brutish.\""],[3,"When Adawm and Ḥawwah had heard these words from Aluahim, they went their way; praising and worshipping Him with a sorrowful heart."],[4,"And Aluahim ceased to commune with them."]],"9":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah came out of the Cave of Treasures, and went near to the garden gate, and there they stood to look at it, and cried for having come away from it."],[2,"And Adawm and Ḥawwah went from before the gate of the garden to the southern side of it, and found there the water that watered the garden, from the root of the Tree of Life, and that split itself from there into four rivers over the earth."],[3,"Then they came and went near to that water, and looked at it; and saw that it was the water that came forth from under the root of the Tree of Life in the garden."],[4,"And Adawm cried and wailed, and beat his chest, for being severed from the garden; and said to Ḥawwah: -"],[5,"\"Why have you brought on me, on yourself, and on our descendants, so many of these plagues and punishments?\""],[6,"And Ḥawwah said to him, \"What is it you have seen that has caused you to cry and to speak to me in this manner?\""],[7,"And he said to Ḥawwah, \"Do you not see this water that was with us in the garden, that watered the trees of the garden, and flowed out from there?"],[8,"And we, when we were in the garden, did not care about it; but since we came to this strange land, we love it, and turn it to use for our body.\""],[9,"But when Ḥawwah heard these words from him, she cried; and from the soreness of their crying, they fell into that water; and would have put an end to themselves in it, so as never again to return and behold the creation; for when they looked at the work of creation, they felt they must put an end to themselves."]],"10":[[1,"Then Aluahim, merciful and gracious, looked at them thus lying in the water, and close to death, and sent an mal'ak, who brought them out of the water, and laid them on the seashore as dead."],[2,"Then the mal'ak went up to Aluahim, was welcome, and said, \"O Aluahim, Your creatures have breathed their last.\""],[3,"Then Aluahim sent His Word to Adawm and Ḥawwah, who raised them from their death."],[4,"And Adawm said, after he was raised, \"O Aluahim, while we were in the garden we did not require, or care for this water; but since we came to this land we cannot do without it.\""],[5,"Then Aluahim said to Adawm, \"While you were under My command and were a bright mal'ak, you knew not this water."],[6,"But now that you have transgressed My mitsvah, you can not do without water, wherein to wash your body and make it grow; for it is now like that of beasts, and is in want of water.\""],[7,"When Adawm and Ḥawwah heard these words from Aluahim, they cried a bitter cry; and Adawm entreated Aluahim to let him return into the garden, and look at it a second time."],[8,"But Aluahim said to Adawm, \"I have made you a promise; when that promise is fulfilled, I will bring you back into the garden, you and your righteous descendants.\""],[9,"And Aluahim ceased to commune with Adawm."]],"11":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah felt themselves burning with thirst, and heat, and sorrow."],[2,"And Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"We shall not drink of this water, even if we were to die. O Ḥawwah, when this water comes into our inner parts, it will increase our punishments and that of our descendants.\""],[3,"Both Adawm and Ḥawwah then went away from the water, and drank none of it at all; but came and entered the Cave of Treasures."],[4,"But when in it Adawm could not see Ḥawwah; he only heard the noise she made. Neither could she see Adawm, but heard the noise he made."],[5,"Then Adawm cried, in deep affliction, and beat his chest; and he got up and said to Ḥawwah, \"Where are you?\""],[6,"And she said to him, \"Look, I am standing in this darkness.\""],[7,"He then said to her, \"Remember the bright nature in which we lived, when we lived in the garden!"],[8,"O Ḥawwah! Remember the esteem that rested on us in the garden. O Ḥawwah! Remember the trees that overshadowed us in the garden while we moved among them."],[9,"O Ḥawwah! Remember that while we were in the garden, we knew neither night nor day. Think of the Tree of Life, from below which flowed the water, and that shed lustre over us! Remember, O Ḥawwah, the garden land, and the brightness thereof!"],[10,"Think, oh think of that garden in which was no darkness, while we lived in it."],[11,"Whereas no sooner did we come into this Cave of Treasures than darkness surrounded us all around; until we can no longer see each other; and all the pleasure of this life has come to an end.\""]],"12":[[1,"Then Adawm beat his chest, he and Ḥawwah, and they mourned the whole night until the crack of dawn, and they sighed over the length of the night in Miyazia."],[2,"And Adawm beat himself, and threw himself on the ground in the cave, from bitter grief, and because of the darkness, and lay there as dead."],[3,"But Ḥawwah heard the noise he made in falling on the ground. And she felt about for him with her hands, and found him like a corpse."],[4,"Then she was afraid, speechless, and remained by him."],[5,"But the merciful Yahuah looked on the death of Adawm, and on Ḥawwah's silence from fear of the darkness. 6 And the Word of Aluahim came to Adawm and raised him from his death, and opened Ḥawwah's mouth that she might speak."],[7,"Then Adawm stood up in the cave and said, \"O Aluahim, why has light departed from us, and darkness covered us? Why did you leave us in this long darkness? Why do you plague us like this?"],[8,"And this darkness, O Yahuah, where was it before it covered us? It is because of this that we cannot see each other."],[9,"For so long as we were in the garden, we neither saw nor even knew what darkness is. I was not hidden from Ḥawwah, neither was she hidden from me, until now that she cannot see me; and no darkness came over us to separate us from each other."],[10,"But she and I were both in one bright light. I saw her and she saw me. Yet now since we came into this cave, darkness has covered us, and separated us from each other, so that I do not see her, and she does not see me."],[11,"O Yahuah, will You then plague us with this darkness?\""]],"13":[[1,"Then when Aluahim, who is merciful and full of pity, heard Adawm's voice, He said to him: -"],[2,"\"O Adawm, so long as the good mal'ak was obedient to Me, a bright light rested on him and on his hosts."],[3,"But when he transgressed My mitsvah, I deprived him of that bright nature, and he became dark."],[4,"And when he was in the shamayim, in the realms of light, he knew nothing of darkness."],[5,"But he transgressed, and I made him fall from the shamayim onto the earth; and it was this darkness that came over him."],[6,"And on you, O Adawm, while in My garden and obedient to Me, did that bright light rest also."],[7,"But when I heard of your transgression, I deprived you of that bright light. Yet, of My mercy, I did not turn you into darkness, but I made you your body of flesh, over which I spread this skin, in order that it may bear cold and heat."],[8,"If I had let My wrath fall heavily on you, I should have destroyed you; and had I turned you into darkness, it would have been as if I had killed you."],[9,"But in My mercy, I have made you as you are; when you transgressed My mitsvah, O Adawm, I drove you from the garden, and made you come forth into this land; and commanded you to live in this cave; and darkness covered you, as it did over him who transgressed My mitsvah."],[10,"Thus, O Adawm, has this night deceived you. It is not to last forever; but is only of twelve hours; when it is over, daylight will return."],[11,"Sigh not, therefore, neither be moved; and say not in your heart that this darkness is long and drags on wearily; and say not in your heart that I plague you with it."],[12,"Strengthen your heart, and be not afraid. This darkness is not a punishment. But, O Adawm, I have made the day, and have placed the sun in it to give light; in order that you and your children should do your work."],[13,"For I knew you would sin and transgress, and come out into this land. Yet I wouldn't force you, nor be heard over you, nor shut up; nor doom you through your fall; nor through your coming out from light into darkness; nor yet through your coming from the garden into this land."],[14,"For I made you of the light; and I willed to bring out children of light from you and like to you."],[15,"But you did not keep My mitsvah one day; until I had finished the creation and baruk everything in it."],[16,"Then, concerning the tree, I commanded you not to eat of it. Yet I knew that Satan, who deceived himself, would also deceive you."],[17,"So I made known to you by means of the tree, not to come near him. And I told you not to eat of the fruit thereof, nor to taste of it, nor yet to sit under it, nor to yield to it."],[18,"Had I not been and spoken to you, O Adawm, concerning the tree, and had I left you without a mitsvah, and you had sinned - it would have been an offence on My part, for not having given you any order; you would turn around and blame Me for it."],[19,"But I commanded you, and warned you, and you fell. So that My creatures cannot blame Me; but the blame rests on them alone."],[20,"And, O Adawm, I have made the day so that you and your descendants can work and toil in it. And I have made the night for them to rest in it from their work; and for the beasts of the field to go forth by night and look for their food."],[21,"But little of darkness now remains, O Adawm, and daylight will soon appear.\""]],"14":[[1,"Then Adawm said to Aluahim: \"O Yahuah, take You my nephesh, and let me not see this gloom any more; or remove me to some place where there is no darkness.\""],[2,"But Aluahim Yahuah said to Adawm, \"Indeed I say to you, this darkness will pass from you, every day I have determined for you, until the fulfillment of My berith; when I will save you and bring you back again into the garden, into the house of light you long for, in which there is no darkness. I will bring you to it - in the kingdom of shamayim.\""],[3,"Again said Aluahim to Adawm, \"All this misery that you have been made to take on yourself because of your transgression, will not free you from the hand of Satan, and will not save you."],[4,"But I will. When I shall come down from shamayim, and shall become flesh of your descendants, and take on Myself the infirmity from which you suffer, then the darkness that covered you in this cave shall cover Me in the grave, when I am in the flesh of your descendants."],[5,"And I, who am without years, shall be subject to the reckoning of years, of times, of months, and of days, and I shall be reckoned as one of the sons of men, in order to save you.\""],[6,"And Aluahim ceased to commune with Adawm. Reference: Yahuchanon 12:46"]],"15":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah cried and sorrowed by reason of Aluahim's word to them, that they should not return to the garden until the fulfillment of the days decreed on them; but mostly because Aluahim had told them that He should suffer for their yasha."]],"16":[[1,"After this, Adawm and Ḥawwah continued to stand in the cave, praying and crying, until the morning dawned on them."],[2,"And when they saw the light returned to them, they retrained from fear, and strengthened their hearts."],[3,"Then Adawm began to come out of the cave. And when he came to the mouth of it, and stood and turned his face towards the east, and saw the sunrise in glowing rays, and felt the heat thereof on his body, he was afraid of it, and thought in his heart that this flame came forth to plague him."],[4,"He then cried and beat his chest, then he fell on the ground on his face and made his request, saying: -"],[5,"\"O Yahuah, plague me not, neither consume me, nor yet take away my life from the earth.\""],[6,"For he thought the sun was Aluahim."],[7,"Because while he was in the garden and heard the voice of Aluahim and the sound He made in the garden, and feared Him, Adawm never saw the brilliant light of the sun, neither did its flaming heat touch his body."],[8,"Therefore he was afraid of the sun when flaming rays of it reached him. He thought Aluahim meant to plague him therewith all the days He had decreed for him."],[9,"For Adawm also said in his thoughts, as Aluahim did not plague us with darkness, behold, He has caused this sun to rise and to plague us with burning heat."],[10,"But while he was thinking like this in his heart, the Word of Aluahim came to him and said: -"],[11,"\"O Adawm, get up on your feet. This sun is not Aluahim; but it has been created to give light by day, of which I spoke to you in the cave saying, 'that the dawn would come, and there would be light by day.'"],[12,"But I am Aluahim who comforted you in the night.\""],[13,"And Aluahim ceased to commune with Adawm."]],"17":[[1,"The Adawm and Ḥawwah came out at the mouth of the cave, and went towards the garden."],[2,"But as they went near it, before the western gate, from which Satan came when he deceived Adawm and Ḥawwah, they found the serpent that became Satan coming at the gate, and sorrowfully licking the dust, and wiggling on its breast on the ground, by reason of the curse that fell on it from Aluahim."],[3,"And whereas before the serpent was the most exalted of all beasts, now it was changed and become slippery, and the meanest of them all, and it crept on its breast and went on its belly."],[4,"And whereas it was the fairest of all beasts, it had been changed, and was become the ugliest of them all. Instead of feeding on the best food, now it turned to eat the dust. Instead of living, as before, in the best places, now it lived in the dust."],[5,"And, whereas it had been the most beautiful of all beasts, all of which stood dumb at its beauty, it was now abhorred of them."],[6,"And, again, whereas it lived in one beautiful home, to which all other animals came from elsewhere; and where it drank, they drank also of the same; now, after it had become venomous, by reason of Aluahim's curse, all beasts fled from its home, and would not drink of the water it drank; but fled from it."]],"18":[[1,"When the accursed serpent saw Adawm and Ḥawwah, it swelled its head, stood on its tail, and with eyes blood – red, acted like it would kill them."],[2,"It made straight for Ḥawwah, and ran after her; while Adawm standing by, cried because he had no stick in his hand with which to hit the serpent, and did not know how to put it to death. 3 But with a heart burning for Ḥawwah, Adawm approached the serpent, and held it by the tail; when it turned towards him and said to him: -"],[4,"\"O Adawm, because of you and of Ḥawwah, I am slippery, and go on my belly.\" Then with its great strength, it threw down Adawm and Ḥawwah and squeezed them, and tried to kill them."],[5,"But Aluahim sent an mal'ak who threw the serpent away from them, and raised them up."],[6,"Then the Word of Aluahim came to the serpent, and said to it, \"The first time I made you slick, and made you to go on your belly; but I did not deprive you of speech."],[7,"This time, however, you will be mute, and you and your race will speak no more; because, the first time My creatures were ruined because of you, and this time you tried to kill them.\""],[8,"Then the serpent was struck mute, and was no longer able to speak."],[9,"And a ruach blew down from shamayim by the command of Aluahim and carried away the serpent from Adawm and Ḥawwah, and threw it on the seashore where it landed in India."]],"19":[[1,"But Adawm and Ḥawwah cried before Aluahim. And Adawm said to Him: -"],[2,"\"O Yahuah, when I was in the cave, I said this to you, my Yahuah, the beasts of the field would rise and devour me, and cut off my life from the earth.\""],[3,"Then Adawm, because of what had happened to him, beat his chest and fell on the ground like a corpse. Then the Word of Aluahim came to him, who raised him, and said to him,"],[4,"\"O Adawm, not one of these beasts will be able to hurt you; because I have made the beasts and other moving things come to you in the cave. I did not let the serpent come with them because it might have risen against you and made you tremble; and the fear of it should fall into your hearts."],[5,"For I knew that the accursed one is wicked; therefore I would not let it come near you with the other beasts."],[6,"But now strengthen your heart and fear not. I am with you to the end of the days I have determined on you.\""]],"20":[[1,"Then Adawm cried and said, \"O Aluahim, take us away to some other place, where the serpent can not come near us again, and rise against us. For fear that it might find Your handmaid Ḥawwah alone and kill her; for its eyes are hideous and evil.\""],[2,"But Aluahim said to Adawm and Ḥawwah, \"From now on, don't be afraid, I will not let it come near you; I have driven it away from you, from this mountain; neither will I leave in it the ability to hurt you.\""],[3,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah worshipped before Aluahim and gave Him thanks, and praised Him for having delivered them from death."]],"21":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah went in search of the garden."],[2,"And the heat beat like a flame on their faces; and they sweated from the heat, and cried before Yahuah."],[3,"But the place where they cried was close to a high mountain, facing the western gate of the garden."],[4,"Then Adawm threw himself down from the top of that mountain; his face was torn and his flesh was ripped; he lost a lot of blood and was close to death."],[5,"Meanwhile Ḥawwah remained standing on the mountain crying over him, thus lying."],[6,"And she said, \"I don't wish to live after him; for all that he did to himself was through me.\""],[7,"Then she threw herself after him; and was torn and ripped by stones; and remained lying as dead."],[8,"But the merciful Aluahim, who looks over His creatures, looked at Adawm and Ḥawwah as they lay dead, and He sent His Word to them, and raised them."],[9,"And said to Adawm, \"O Adawm, all this misery which you have brought on yourself, will have no affect against My rule, neither will it alter the berith of the 5,"]],"22":[[1,"Then Adawm said to Aluahim, \"I dry up in the heat, I am faint from walking, and I don't want to be in this world. And I don't know when You will take me out of it to rest.\""],[2,"Then Yahuah Aluahim said to him, \"O Adawm, it cannot be now, not until you have ended your days. Then shall I bring you out of this miserable land.\""],[3,"And Adawm said to Aluahim, \"While I was in the garden I knew neither heat, nor languor, neither moving about, nor trembling, nor fear; but now since I came to this land, all this affliction has come over me."],[4,"Then Aluahim said to Adawm, \"So long as you were keeping My mitsvah, My light and My chen rested on you. But when you transgressed My mitsvah, sorrow and misery came to you in this land.\""],[5,"And Adawm cried and said, \"O Yahuah, do not cut me off for this, neither punish me with heavy plagues, nor yet repay me according to my sin; for we, of our own will, transgressed Your mitsvah, and ignored Your law, and tried to become Aluahims like you, when Satan the enemy deceived us.\""],[6,"Then Aluahim said again to Adawm, \"Because you have endured fear and trembling in this land, languor and suffering, treading and walking about, going on this mountain, and dying from it, I will take all this on Myself in order to save you.\""]],"23":[[1,"Then Adawm cried more and said, \"O Aluahim, have mercy on me, so far as to take on yourself, that which I will do.\""],[2,"But Aluahim withdrew His Word from Adawm and Ḥawwah."],[3,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah stood on their feet; and Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Strengthen yourself, and I also will strengthen myself.\" And she strengthened herself, as Adawm told her."],[4,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah took stones and placed them in the shape of an mizbe'ach; and they took leaves from the trees outside the garden, with which they wiped, from the face of the rock, the blood they had spilled."],[5,"But that which had dropped on the sand, they took together with the dust with which it was mingled and offered it on the mizbe'ach as an offering to Aluahim."],[6,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah stood under the Mizbe'ach and cried, thus praying to Aluahim, \"Forgive us our trespass and our sin, and look at us with Thine eye of mercy. For when we were in the garden our praises and our hymns went up before you without ceasing."],[7,"But when we came into this strange land, pure praise was not longer ours, nor righteous prayer, nor understanding hearts, nor sweet thoughts, nor just counsels, nor long discernment, nor upright feelings, neither is our bright nature left us. But our body is changed from the likeness in which it was at first, when we were created."],[8,"Yet now look at our blood which is offered on these stones, and accept it at our hands, like the praise we used to sing to you at first, when in the garden.\""],[9,"And Adawm began to make more requests of Aluahim. ORIGINAL OF YAHUAH'S PRAYER SAID TO BE USED ABOUT"]],"24":[[1,"Then the merciful Aluahim, good and lover of men, looked at Adawm and Ḥawwah, and at their blood, which they had held up as an offering to Him; without an order from Him for so doing. But He wondered at them; and accepted their offerings."],[2,"And Aluahim sent from His presence a bright fire, that consumed their offering."],[3,"He smelled the sweet savor of their offering, and showed them mercy."],[4,"Then came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm, and said to him, \"O Adawm, as you have shed your blood, so will I shed My own blood when I become flesh of your descendants; and as you died, O Adawm, so also will I die. And as you built an mizbe'ach, so also will I make for you an mizbe'ach of the earth; and as you offered your blood on it, so also will I offer My blood on an mizbe'ach on the earth."],[5,"And as you sued for forgiveness through that blood, so also will I make My blood forgiveness of sins, and erase transgressions in it."],[6,"And now, behold, I have accepted your offering, O Adawm, but the days of the berith in which I have bound you are not fulfilled. When they are fulfilled, then will I bring you back into the garden."],[7,"Now, therefore, strengthen your heart; and when sorrow comes over you, make Me an offering, and I will be favorable to you.\""]],"25":[[1,"But Aluahim knew that Adawm believed he should frequently kill himself and make an offering to Him of his blood."],[2,"Therefore He said to him, \"O Adawm, don't ever kill yourself like this again, by throwing yourself down from that mountain.\""],[3,"But Adawm said to Aluahim, \"I was thinking to put an end to myself at once, for having transgressed Your mitsvot, and for my having come out of the beautiful garden; and for the bright light of which You have deprived me; and for the praises which poured forth from my mouth without ceasing, and for the light that covered me."],[4,"Yet of Your goodness, O Aluahim, do not get rid of me altogether; but be favorable to me every time I die, and bring me to life."],[5,"And thereby it will be made known that You are a merciful Aluahim, who does not want anyone to perish; who loves not that one should fall; and who does not condemn any one cruelly, badly, and by whole destruction.\""],[6,"Then Adawm remained silent."],[7,"And the Word of Aluahim came to him, and baruk him, and comforted him, and covenanted with him, that He would save him at the end of the days determined for him."],[8,"This, then, was the first offering Adawm made to Aluahim; and so it became his custom to do."]],"26":[[1,"Then Adawm took Ḥawwah, and they began to return to the Cave of Treasures where they lived. But when they got closer to it and saw it from a distance, heavy sorrow fell on Adawm and Ḥawwah when they looked at it."],[2,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"When we were on the mountain we were comforted by the Word of Aluahim that conversed with us; and the light that came from the east shown over us."],[3,"But now the Word of Aluahim is hidden from us; and the light that shown over us is so changed as to disappear, and let darkness and sorrow come over us."],[4,"And we are forced to enter this cave which is like a prison, in which darkness covers us, so that we are separated from each other; and you can not see me, neither can I see you.\""],[5,"When Adawm had said these words, they cried and spread their hands before Aluahim; for they were full of sorrow."],[6,"And they prayed to Aluahim to bring the sun to them, to shine on them, so that darkness would not return to them, and that they wouldn't have to go under this covering of rock. And they wished to die rather than see the darkness."],[7,"Then Aluahim looked at Adawm and Ḥawwah and at their great sorrow, and at all they had done with a fervent heart, on account of all the trouble they were in, instead of their former well-being, and on account of all the misery that came over them in a strange land."],[8,"Therefore Aluahim was not angry with them; nor impatient with them; but he was patient and forbearing towards them, as towards the children He had created."],[9,"Then came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm, and said to him, \"Adawm, as for the sun, if I were to take it and bring it to you, days, hours, years and months would all stop, and the berith I have made with you, would never be fulfilled."],[10,"But then you would be deserted and stuck in a perpetual plague, and you would never be saved. 11 Yes, rather, bear long and calm your nephesh while you live night and day; until the fulfillment of the days, and the time of My berith is come."],[12,"Then shall I come and save you, O Adawm, for I do not wish that you be afflicted."],[13,"And when I look at all the good things in which you lived, and why you came out of them, then would I willingly show you mercy."],[14,"But I cannot alter the berith that has gone out of My mouth; otherwise I would have brought you back into the garden."],[15,"When, however, the berith is fulfilled, then shall I show you and your descendants mercy, and bring you into a land of gladness, where there is neither sorrow nor suffering; but abiding joy and gladness, and light that never fails, and praises that never cease; and a beautiful garden that shall never pass away.\""],[16,"And Aluahim said again to Adawm, \"Be patient and enter the cave, for the darkness, of which you were afraid, shall only be twelve hours long; and when ended, light shall come up.\""],[17,"Then when Adawm heard these words from Aluahim, he and Ḥawwah worshipped before Him, and their hearts were comforted. They returned into the cave after their custom, while tears flowed from their eyes, sorrow and wailing came from their hearts, and they wished their nephesh would leave their body."],[18,"And Adawm and Ḥawwah stood praying until the darkness of night came over them, and Adawm was hid from Ḥawwah, and she from him."],[19,"And they remained standing in prayer."]],"27":[[1,"When Satan, the hater of all good, saw how they continued in prayer, and how Aluahim communed with them, and comforted them, and how He had accepted their offering - Satan made an apparition."],[2,"He began with transforming his hosts; in his hands was a flashing fire, and they were in a great light."],[3,"He then placed his throne near the mouth of the cave because he could not enter into it by reason of their prayers. And he shed light into the cave, until the cave glistened over Adawm and Ḥawwah; while his hosts began to sing praises."],[4,"And Satan did this, in order that when Adawm saw the light, he should think within himself that it was a heavenly light, and that Satan's hosts were mal'akim; and that Aluahim had sent them to watch at the cave, and to give him light in the darkness."],[5,"So that when Adawm came out of the cave and saw them, and Adawm and Ḥawwah bowed to Satan, then he would overcome Adawm thereby, and a second time humble him before Aluahim."],[6,"When, therefore, Adawm and Ḥawwah saw the light, fancying it was real, they strengthened their hearts; yet, as they were trembling, Adawm said to Ḥawwah: -"],[7,"\"Look at that great light, and at those many songs of praise, and at that host standing outside who won't come into our cave. Why don't they tell us what they want, where they are from, what the meaning of this light is, what those praises are, why they have been sent to this place, and why they won't come in?"],[8,"If they were from Aluahim, they would come into the cave with us, and would tell us why they were sent.\""],[9,"Then Adawm stood up and prayed to Aluahim with a burning heart, and said: -"],[10,"\"O Yahuah, is there in the world another Aluahim besides You, who created mal'akim and filled them with light, and sent them to keep us, who would come with them?"],[11,"But, look, we see these hosts that stand at the mouth of the cave; they are in a great light; they sing loud praises. If they are of some other Aluahim than You, tell me; and if they are sent by you, inform me of the reason for which You have sent them.\""],[12,"No sooner had Adawm said this, than an mal'ak from Aluahim appeared to him in the cave, who said to him, \"O Adawm, fear not. This is Satan and his hosts; he wishes to deceive you as he deceived you at first. For the first time, he was hidden in the serpent; but this time he is come to you in the likeness of an mal'ak of light; in order that, when you worshipped him, he might enslave you, in the very presence of Aluahim.\""],[13,"Then the mal'ak went from Adawm and seized Satan at the opening of the cave, and stripped him of the pretense he had assumed, and brought him in his own hideous form to Adawm and Ḥawwah; who were afraid of him when they saw him."],[14,"And the mal'ak said to Adawm, \"This hideous form has been his ever since Aluahim made him fall from shamayim. He could not have come near you in it; he therefore transformed himself into an mal'ak of light.\""],[15,"Then the mal'ak drove away Satan and his hosts from Adawm and Ḥawwah, and said to them, \"Fear not; Aluahim who created you, will strengthen you.\""],[16,"And the mal'ak left them."],[17,"But Adawm and Ḥawwah remained standing in the cave; no consolation came to them; they divided in their thoughts."],[18,"And when it was morning they prayed; and then went out to seek the garden. For their hearts were towards it, and they could get no consolation for having left it."]],"28":[[1,"But when the crafty Satan saw them, that they were going to the garden, he gathered together his host, and came in appearance on a cloud, intent on deceiving them."],[2,"But when Adawm and Ḥawwah saw him thus in a vision, they thought they were mal'akim of Aluahim come to comfort them about having left the garden, or to bring them back again into it."],[3,"And Adawm spread his hands before Aluahim, beseeching Him to make him understand what they were."],[4,"Then Satan, the hater of all good, said to Adawm, \"O Adawm, I am an mal'ak of the great Aluahim; and, behold the hosts that surround me."],[5,"Aluahim has sent us to take you and bring you to the border of the garden northwards; to the shore of the clear sea, and bathe you and Ḥawwah in it, and raise you to your former gladness, that you return again to the garden.\""],[6,"These words sank into the heart of Adawm and Ḥawwah."],[7,"Yet Aluahim withheld His Word from Adawm, and did not make him understand at once, but waited to see his strength; whether he would be overcome as Ḥawwah was when in the garden, or whether he would prevail."],[8,"Then Satan called to Adawm and Ḥawwah, and said, \"Behold, we go to the sea of water,\" and they began to go."],[9,"And Adawm and Ḥawwah followed them at some little distance."],[10,"But when they came to the mountain to the north of the garden, a very high mountain, without any steps to the top of it, the Devil drew near to Adawm and Ḥawwah, and made them go up to the top in reality, and not in a vision; wishing, as he did, to throw them down and kill them, and to wipe off their name from the earth; so that this earth should remain to him and his hosts alone."]],"29":[[1,"But when the merciful Aluahim saw that Satan wished to kill Adawm with his many tricks, and saw that Adawm was meek and without guile, Aluahim spoke to Satan in a loud voice, and cursed him."],[2,"Then he and his hosts fled, and Adawm and Ḥawwah remained standing on the top of the mountain, from there they saw below them the wide world, high above which they were. But they saw none of the host which time after time were by them."],[3,"They cried, both Adawm and Ḥawwah, before Aluahim, and begged for forgiveness of Him."],[4,"Then came the Word from Aluahim to Adawm, and said to him, \"Know you and understand concerning this Satan, that he seeks to deceive you and your descendants after you.\""],[5,"And Adawm cried before Yahuah Aluahim, and begged and prayed to Him to give him something from the garden, as a token to him, wherein to be comforted."],[6,"And Aluahim considered Adawm's thought, and sent the mal'ak Michaal as far as the sea that reaches India, to take from there golden rods and bring them to Adawm."],[7,"This did Aluahim in His wisdom in order that these golden rods, being with Adawm in the cave, should shine forth with light in the night around him, and put an end to his fear of the darkness."],[8,"Then the mal'ak Michaal went down by Aluahim's order, took golden rods, as Aluahim had commanded him, and brought them to Aluahim."]],"30":[[1,"After these things, Aluahim commanded the mal'ak Gabrial to go down to the garden, and say to the cherub who kept it, \"Behold, Aluahim has commanded me to come into the garden, and to take from it sweet smelling incense, and give it to Adawm.\""],[2,"Then the mal'ak Gabrial went down by Aluahim's order to the garden, and told the cherub as Aluahim had commanded him."],[3,"The cherub then said, \"Well.\" And Gabrial went in and took the incense."],[4,"Then Aluahim commanded his mal'ak Raphaal to go down to the garden, and speak to the cherub about some myrrh, to give to Adawm."],[5,"And the mal'ak Raphaal went down and told the cherub as Aluahim had commanded him, and the cherub said, \"Well.\" Then Raphaal went in and took the myrrh."],[6,"The golden rods were from the Indian sea, where there are precious stones. The incense was from the eastern border of the garden; and the myrrh from the western border, from where bitterness came over Adawm."],[7,"And the mal'akim brought these things to Aluahim, by the Tree of Life, in the garden."],[8,"Then Aluahim said to the mal'akim, \"Dip them in the spring of water; then take them and sprinkle their water over Adawm and Ḥawwah, that they be a little comforted in their sorrow, and give them to Adawm and Ḥawwah."],[9,"And the mal'akim did as Aluahim had commanded them, and they gave all those things to Adawm and Ḥawwah on the top of the mountain on which Satan had placed them, when he sought to make an end of them."],[10,"And when Adawm saw the golden rods, the incense and the myrrh, he was rejoiced and cried because he thought that the gold was a token of the kingdom from where he had come, that the incense was a token of the bright light which had been taken from him, and that the myrrh was a token of the sorrow in which he was."]],"31":[[1,"After these things Aluahim said to Adawm, \"You asked Me for something from the garden, to be comforted therewith, and I have given you these three tokens as a consolation to you; that you trust in Me and in My berith with you."],[2,"For I will come and save you; and kings shall bring me when in the flesh, gold, incense and myrrh; gold as a token of My kingdom; incense as a token of My Aluahim; and myrrh as a token of My suffering and of My death."],[3,"But, O Adawm, put these by you in the cave; the gold that it may shed light over you by night; the incense, that you smell its sweet savor; and the myrrh, to comfort you in your sorrow.\""],[4,"When Adawm heard these words from Aluahim, he worshipped before Him. He and Ḥawwah worshipped Him and gave Him thanks, because He had dealt mercifully with them."],[5,"Then Aluahim commanded the three mal'akim, Michaal, Gabrial and Raphaal, each to bring what he had brought, and give it to Adawm. And they did so, one by one."],[6,"And Aluahim commanded Suriyal and Salathial to bear up Adawm and Ḥawwah, and bring them down from the top of the high mountain, and to take them to the Cave of Treasures."],[7,"There they laid the gold on the south side of the cave, the incense on the eastern side, and the myrrh on the western side. For the mouth of the cave was on the north side."],[8,"The mal'akim then comforted Adawm and Ḥawwah, and departed."],[9,"The gold was seventy rods; the incense, twelve pounds; and the myrrh, three pounds."],[10,"These remained by Adawm in the Cave of Treasures."],[11,"Aluahim gave these three things to Adawm on the third day after he had come out of the garden, in token of the three days Yahuah should remain in the heart of the earth."],[12,"And these three things, as they continued with Adawm in the cave, gave him light by night; and by day they gave him a little relief from his sorrow. A rod is a unit of linear measure equivalent to 5.5 yards and also a unit of area measure equivalent to 30.25 square yards. In this case, the word rod simply means a kind of long, thin piece of gold of unspecified size and weight. This is the original text which appears to contain embedded editorial content: \"These remained by Adawm in the House of Treasures; therefore was it called 'of concealment.' But other interpreters say it was called the 'Cave of Treasures,' by reason of the bodies of righteous men that were in it."]],"32":[[1,"And Adawm and Ḥawwah remained in the Cave of Treasures until the seventh day; they neither ate of the fruit the earth, nor drank water."],[2,"And when it dawned on the eighth day, Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"O Ḥawwah, we prayed Aluahim to give us something from the garden, and He sent his mal'akim who brought us what we had desired."],[3,"But now, get up, let us go to the sea of water we saw at first, and let us stand in it, praying that Aluahim will again be favorable to us and take us back to the garden; or give us something; or that He will give us comfort in some other land than this in which we are.\""],[4,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah came out of the cave, went and stood on the border of the sea in which they had before thrown themselves, and Adawm said to Ḥawwah: -"],[5,"Come, go down into this place, and come not out of it until the end of thirty days, when I shall come to you. And pray to Aluahim with burning heart and a sweet voice, to forgive us."],[6,"And I will go to another place, and go down into it, and do like you.\""],[7,"Then Ḥawwah went down into the water, as Adawm had commanded her. Adawm also went down into the water; and they stood praying; and besought Yahuah to forgive them their offense, and to restore them to their former state."],[8,"And they stood like that praying, until the end of the thirty-five days."]],"33":[[1,"But Satan, the hater of all good, sought them in the cave, but found them not, although he searched diligently for them."],[2,"But he found them standing in the water praying and thought within himself, \"Adawm and Ḥawwah are standing like that in that water praying to Aluahim to forgive them their transgression, and to restore them to their former state, and to take them from under my hand."],[3,"But I will deceive them so that they shall come out of the water, and not fulfil their vow.\""],[4,"Then the hater of all good, went not to Adawm, but he went to Ḥawwah, and took the form of an mal'ak of Aluahim, praising and rejoicing, and said to her: -"],[5,"\"Shalom be to you! Be glad and rejoice! Aluahim is favorable to you, and He sent me to Adawm. I have brought him the glad tidings of yasha, and of his being filled with bright light as he was at first."],[6,"And Adawm, in his joy for his restoration, has sent me to you, that you come to me, in order that I crown you with light like him."],[7,"And he said to me, 'Speak to Ḥawwah; if she does not come with you, tell her of the sign when we were on the top of the mountain; how Aluahim sent his mal'akim who took us and brought us to the Cave of Treasures; and laid the gold on the southern side; incense, on the eastern side; and myrrh on the western side.' Now come to him.\""],[8,"When Ḥawwah hear these words from him, she rejoiced greatly. And thinking Satan's appearance was real, she came out of the sea."],[9,"He went before, and she followed him until they came to Adawm. Then Satan hid himself from her, and she saw him no more."],[10,"She then came and stood before Adawm, who was standing by the water and rejoicing in Aluahim's forgiveness."],[11,"And as she called to him, he turned around, found her there and cried when he saw her, and beat his chest; and from the bitterness of his grief, he sank into the water."],[12,"But Aluahim looked at him and at his misery, and at his being about to breathe his last. And the Word of Aluahim came from shamayim, raised him out of the water, and said to him, \"Go up the high bank to Ḥawwah.\" And when he came up to Ḥawwah he said to her, \"Who told you to come here?\""],[13,"Then she told him the discourse of the mal'ak who had appeared to her and had given her a sign."],[14,"But Adawm grieved, and gave her to know it was Satan. He then took her and they both returned to the cave."],[15,"These things happened to them the second time they went down to the water, seven days after their coming out of the garden."],[16,"They fasted in the water thirty-five days; altogether forty-two days since they had left the garden."]],"34":[[1,"And on the morning of the forty-third day, they came out of the cave, sorrowful and crying. Their bodies were lean, and they were parched from hunger and thirst, from fasting and praying, and from their heavy sorrow on account of their transgression."],[2,"And when they had come out of the cave they went up the mountain to the west of the garden."],[3,"There they stood and prayed and besought Aluahim to grant them forgiveness of their sins."],[4,"And after their prayers Adawm began to beg Aluahim, saying, \"O my Yahuah, my Aluahim, and my Creator, You commanded the four elements to be gathered together, and they were gathered together by Thine order."],[5,"Then You spread Your hand and created me out of one element, that of dust of the earth; and You brought me into the garden at the third hour, on a Friday, and informed me of it in the cave."],[6,"Then, at first, I knew neither night nor day, for I had a bright nature; neither did the light in which I lived ever leave me to know night or day."],[7,"Then, again, O Yahuah, in that third hour in which You created me, You brought to me all beasts, and lions, and ostriches, and fowls of the air, and all things that move in the earth, which You had created at the first hour before me of the Friday."],[8,"And Your will was that I should name them all, one by one, with a suitable name. But You gave me understanding and knowledge, and a pure heart and a right mind from you, that I should name them after Thine own mind regarding the naming of them."],[9,"O Aluahim, You made them obedient to me, and ordered that not one of them break from my sway, according to Your mitsvah, and to the dominion which You had given me over them. But now they are all estranged from me."],[10,"Then it was in that third hour of Friday, in which You created me, and commanded me concerning the tree, to which I was neither to go near, nor to eat thereof; for You said to me in the garden, 'When you eat of it, of death you shall die.'"],[11,"And if You had punished me as You said, with death, I should have died that very moment."],[12,"Moreover, when You commanded me regarding the tree, I was neither to approach nor to eat thereof, Ḥawwah was not with me; You had not yet created her, neither had You yet taken her out of my side; nor had she yet heard this order from you."],[13,"Then, at the end of the third hour of that Friday, O Yahuah, You caused a slumber and a sleep to come over me, and I slept, and was overwhelmed in sleep."],[14,"Then You drew a rib out of my side, and created it after my own likeness and image. Then I awoke; and when I saw her and knew who she was, I said, 'This is bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh; from now on she shall be called woman.'"],[15,"It was of Your good will, O Aluahim, that You brought a slumber in a sleep over me, and that You immediately brought Ḥawwah out of my side, until she was out, so that I did not see how she was made; neither could I witness, O my Yahuah, how awful and great are Your goodness and esteem."],[16,"And of Your goodwill, O Yahuah, You made us both with bodies of a bright nature, and You made us two, one; and You gave us Your chen, and filled us with praises of the Ruach HaQadash; that we should be neither hungry nor thirsty, nor know what sorrow is, nor yet faintness of heart; neither suffering, fasting nor weariness."],[17,"But now, O Aluahim, since we transgressed Your mitsvah and broke Your law, You have brought us out into a strange land, and have caused suffering, and faintness, hunger and thirst to come over us."],[18,"Now, therefore, O Aluahim, we pray you, give us something to eat from the garden, to satisfy our hunger with it; and something wherewith to quench our thirst."],[19,"For, behold, many days, O Aluahim, we have tasted nothing and drunk nothing, and our flesh is dried up, and our strength is wasted, and sleep is gone from our eyes from faintness and crying."],[20,"Then, O Aluahim, we dare not gather anything from the fruit of trees, from fear of you. For when we transgress at first You spared us and did not make us die."],[21,"But now, we thought in our hearts, if we eat of the fruit of the trees, without Aluahim's order, He will destroy us this time, and will wipe us off from the face of the earth."],[22,"And if we drink of this water, without Aluahim's order, He will make an end of us and root us up at once."],[23,"Now, therefore, O Aluahim, that I am come to this place with Ḥawwah, we beg You to give us some fruit from the garden, that we may be satisfied with it."],[24,"For we desire the fruit that is on the earth, and all else that we lack in it.\" The medieval belief that there were only four elements fire, earth, air, and water was widely accepted until about 1500 AD when the current atomic theory was in its infancy."]],"35":[[1,"Then Aluahim looked again at Adawm and his crying and groaning, and the Word of Aluahim came to him, and said to him: -"],[2,"\"O Adawm, when you were in My garden, you knew neither eating nor drinking; neither faintness nor suffering; neither leanness of flesh, nor change; neither did sleep depart from thine eyes. But since you transgressed, and came into this strange land, all these trials are come over you.\""]],"36":[[1,"Then Aluahim commanded the cherub, who kept the gate of the garden with a sword of fire in his hand, to take some of the fruit of the fig-tree, and to give it to Adawm."],[2,"The cherub obeyed the command of Yahuah Aluahim, and went into the garden and brought two figs on two twigs, each fig hanging to its leaf; they were from two of the trees among which Adawm and Ḥawwah hid themselves when Aluahim went to walk in the garden, and the Word of Aluahim came to Adawm and Ḥawwah and said to them, \"Adawm, Adawm, where are you?\""],[3,"And Adawm answered, \"O Aluahim, here I am. When I heard the sound of You and Your voice, I hid myself, because I am naked.\""],[4,"Then the cherub took two figs and brought them to Adawm and Ḥawwah. But he threw them to them from a distance; for they might not come near the cherub by reason of their flesh, that could not come near the fire."],[5,"At first, mal'akim trembled at the presence of Adawm and were afraid of him. But now Adawm trembled before the mal'akim and was afraid of them."],[6,"Then Adawm came closer and took one fig, and Ḥawwah also came in turn and took the other."],[7,"And as they took them up in their hands, they looked at them, and knew they were from the trees among which they had hidden themselves."]],"37":[[1,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Do you not see these figs and their leaves, with which we covered ourselves when we were stripped of our bright nature? But now, we do not know what misery and suffering may come over us from eating them."],[2,"Now, therefore, O Ḥawwah, let us restrain ourselves and not eat of them, you and I; and let us ask Aluahim to give us of the fruit of the Tree of Life.\""],[3,"Thus did Adawm and Ḥawwah restrain themselves, and did not eat of these figs."],[4,"But Adawm began to pray to Aluahim and to beseech Him to give him of the fruit of the Tree of Life, saying thus: \"O Aluahim, when we transgressed Your mitsvah at the sixth hour of Friday, we were stripped of the bright nature we had, and did not continue in the garden after our transgression, more than three hours."],[5,"But in the evening You made us come out of it. O Aluahim, we transgressed against You one hour, and all these trials and sorrows have come over us until this day."],[6,"And those days together with this the forty-third day, do not redeem that one hour in which we transgressed!"],[7,"O Aluahim, look at us with an eye of pity, and do not avenge us according to our transgression of Your mitsvah, in Your presence."],[8,"O Aluahim, give us of the fruit of the Tree of Life, that we may eat of it, and live, and turn not to see sufferings and other trouble, in this earth; for You are Aluahim."],[9,"When we transgressed Your mitsvah, You made us come out of the garden, and sent a cherub to keep the Tree of Life, lest we should eat thereof, and live; and know nothing of faintness after we transgressed."],[10,"But now, O Yahuah, behold, we have endured all these days, and have borne sufferings. Make these forty-three days an equivalent for the one hour in which we transgressed.\""]],"38":[[1,"After these things the Word of Aluahim came to Adawm, and said to him: -"],[2,"\"O Adawm, as to the fruit on the Tree of Life that you have asked for, I will not give it to you now, but only when the 5500 years are fulfilled. At that time I will give you fruit from the Tree of Life, and you will eat, and live forever, you, and Ḥawwah, and your righteous descendants."],[3,"But these forty-three days cannot make amends for the hour in which you transgressed My mitsvah."],[4,"O Adawm, I gave you the fruit of the fig-tree to eat in which you hid yourself. Go and eat of it, you and Ḥawwah."],[5,"I will not deny your request, neither will I disappoint your hope; therefore, endure until the fulfillment of the berith I made with you.\""],[6,"And Aluahim withdrew His Word from Adawm."]],"39":[[1,"Then Adawm returned to Ḥawwah, and said to her, \"Get up, and take a fig for yourself, and I will take another; and let us go to our cave.\""],[2,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah took each a fig and went towards the cave; the time was about the setting of the sun; and their thoughts made them long to eat of the fruit."],[3,"But Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"I am afraid to eat of this fig. I know not what may come over me from it.\""],[4,"So Adawm cried, and stood praying before Aluahim, saying, \"Satisfy my hunger, without my having to eat this fig; for after I have eaten it, what will it profit me? And what shall I desire and ask of you, O Aluahim, when it is gone?\""],[5,"And he said again, \"I am afraid to eat of it; for I know not what will befall me through it.\""]],"40":[[1,"Then the Word of Aluahim came to Adawm, and said to him, \"O Adawm, why didn't you have this dread, or this fasting, or this care before now? And why didn't you have this fear before you transgressed?"],[2,"But when you came to live in this strange land, your animal body could not survive on earth without earthly food, to strengthen it and to restore its powers.\""],[3,"And Aluahim withdrew His Word for Adawm."]],"41":[[1,"Then Adawm took the fig, and laid it on the golden rods. Ḥawwah also took her fig, and put it on the incense. 2 And the weight of each fig was that of a water-melon; for the fruit of the garden was much larger than the fruit of this land."],[3,"But Adawm and Ḥawwah remained standing and fasting the whole of that night, until the morning dawned."],[4,"When the sun rose they were still praying, but after they had finished praying, Adawm said to Ḥawwah: -"],[5,"\"O Ḥawwah, come, let us go to the border of the garden looking south; to the place from where the river flows, and is parted into four heads. There we will pray to Aluahim, and ask Him to give us some of the Water of Life to drink."],[6,"For Aluahim has not fed us with the Tree of Life, in order that we may not live. Therefore, we will ask him to give us some of the Water of Life, and to quench our thirst with it, rather than with a drink of water of this land.\""],[7,"When Ḥawwah heard these words from Adawm, she agreed; and they both got up and came to the southern border of the garden, at the edge of the river of water a short distance from the garden."],[8,"And they stood and prayed before Yahuah, and asked Him to look at them this once, to forgive them, and to grant them their request."],[9,"After this prayer from both of them, Adawm began to pray with his voice before Aluahim, and said; -"],[10,"\"O Yahuah, when I was in the garden and saw the water that flowed from under the Tree of Life, my heart did not desire, neither did my body require to drink of it; neither did I know thirst, for I was living; and above that which I am now."],[11,"So that in order to live I did not require any Food of Life, neither did I drink of the Water of Life."],[12,"But now, O Aluahim, I am dead; my flesh is parched with thirst. Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink of it and live."],[13,"Of Your mercy, O Aluahim, save me from these plagues and trials, and bring me into another land different from this, if You will not let me live in Your garden.\" This is substantiated by Genesis 3:7 whereby the leaves of the fig tree were large enough that Adawm and Ḥawwah could fashion garments from them."]],"42":[[1,"Then came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm, and said to him: -"],[2,"\"O Adawm, as to what you said, 'Bring me into a land where there is rest,' it is not another land than this, but it is the kingdom of shamayim where alone there is rest."],[3,"But you can not make your entrance into it at present; but only after your mishpat is past and fulfilled."],[4,"Then will I make you go up into the kingdom of shamayim, you and your righteous descendants; and I will give you and them the rest you ask for at present."],[5,"And if you said, 'Give me of the Water of Life that I may drink and live' - it cannot be this day, but on the day that I shall descend into Sheol, and break the gates of brass, and bruise in pieces the kingdoms of iron."],[6,"Then will I in mercy save your nephesh and the nepheshoth of the righteous, to give them rest in My garden. And that shall be when the end of the world is come."],[7,"And, again, in regards to the Water of Life you seek, it will not be granted you this day; but on the day that I shall shed My blood on your head in the land of Golgotha."],[8,"For My blood shall be the Water of Life to you at that time, and not to just you alone, but to all your descendants who shall believe in Me; that it be to them for rest forever.\""],[9,"Yahuah said again to Adawm, \"O Adawm, when you were in the garden, these trials did not come to you."],[10,"But since you transgressed My mitsvah, all these sufferings have come over you."],[11,"Now, also, does your flesh require food and drink; drink then of that water that flows by you on the face of the earth."],[12,"Then Aluahim withdrew His Word from Adawm."],[13,"And Adawm and Ḥawwah worshipped Yahuah, and returned from the river of water to the cave. It was noon-day; and when they drew near to the cave, they saw a large fire by it. This phrase indicates that the bleeding will take place in an Alevated position above the populace. This is believed to be a reference to the stake whereby Mashiach bled profusely above the people below. Golgotha (goal-goth-uh) was the hill outside the walls of Yahrushalayim where Yahusha was impaled. Its exact location is not precisely known, but the Church of the Holy Sepulcher is believed to have been constructed on this hill. Reference: Yahuchanon 6:25 and 7:38"]],"43":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah were afraid, and stood still. And Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"What is that fire by our cave? We have done nothing in it to cause this fire."],[2,"We neither have bread to bake therein, nor broth to cook there. As to this fire, we have never known anything like it, neither do we know what to call it. 3 But ever since Aluahim sent the cherub with a sword of fire that flashed and lightened in his hand, from fear of which we fell down and were like corpses, have we not seen the like."],[4,"But now, O Ḥawwah, behold, this is the same fire that was in the cherub's hand, which Aluahim has sent to keep the cave in which we live."],[5,"O Ḥawwah, it is because Aluahim is angry with us, and will drive us from it."],[6,"O Ḥawwah, we have again transgressed His mitsvah in that cave, so that He had sent this fire to burn around it, and to prevent us from going into it."],[7,"If this be really so, O Ḥawwah, where shall we live? And where shall we flee from before the face of Yahuah? Since, in regards to the garden, He will not let us live in it, and He has deprived us of the good things thereof; but He has placed us in this cave, in which we have borne darkness, trials and hardships, until at last we have found comfort therein."],[8,"But now that He has brought us out into another land, who knows what may happen in it? And who knows but that the darkness of that land may be far greater than the darkness of this land?"],[9,"Who knows what may happen in that land by day or by night? And who knows whether it will be far or near, O Ḥawwah? Where it will please Aluahim to put us, may be far from the garden, O Ḥawwah? Or where Aluahim will prevent us from beholding Him, because we have transgressed His mitsvah, and because we have made requests of Him at all times? 10 O Ḥawwah, if Aluahim will bring us into a strange land other than this, in which we find consolation, it must be to put our nepheshoth to death, and blot out our name from the face of the earth."],[11,"O Ḥawwah, if we are further alienated from the garden and from Aluahim, where shall we find Him again, and ask Him to give us gold, incense, myrrh, and some fruit of the fig-tree?"],[12,"Where shall we find Him, to comfort us a second time? Where shall we find Him, that He may think of us, as regards the berith He has made on our behalf?\""],[13,"Then Adawm said no more. And they kept looking, He and Ḥawwah, towards the cave, and at the fire that flared up around it."],[14,"But that fire was from Satan. For he had gathered trees and dry grasses, and had carried and brought them to the cave, and had set fire to them, in order to consume the cave and what was in it."],[15,"So that Adawm and Ḥawwah should be left in sorrow, and he should cut off their trust in Aluahim, and make them deny Him."],[16,"But by the mercy of Aluahim he could not burn the cave, for Aluahim sent His mal'ak around the cave to guard it from such a fire, until it went out."],[17,"And this fire lasted from noon-day until the break of day. That was the forty-fifth day."]],"44":[[1,"Yet Adawm and Ḥawwah were standing and looking at the fire, and unable to come near the cave from their dread of the fire."],[2,"And Satan kept on bringing trees and throwing them into the fire, until the flames of the fire rose up on high, and covered the whole cave, thinking, as he did in his own mind, to consume the cave with much fire. But the mal'ak of Yahuah was guarding it."],[3,"And yet he could not curse Satan, nor injure him by word, because he had no authority over him, neither did he take to doing so with words from his mouth."],[4,"Therefore the mal'ak tolerated him, without saying one bad word, until the Word of Aluahim came who said to Satan, \"Go away from here; once before you deceived My servants, and this time you seek to destroy them."],[5,"Were it not for My mercy I would have destroyed you and your hosts from off the earth. But I have had patience with you, until the end of the world.\""],[6,"Then Satan fled from before Yahuah. But the fire went on burning around the cave like a coal-fire the whole day; which was the forty-sixth day Adawm and Ḥawwah had spent since they came out of the garden."],[7,"And when Adawm and Ḥawwah saw that the heat of the fire had somewhat cooled down, they began to walk towards the cave to get into it as they usually did; but they could not, by reason of the heat of the fire."],[8,"Then they both began crying because of the fire that separated them from the cave, and that came towards them, burning. And they were afraid."],[9,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"See this fire of which we have a portion in us: which formerly yielded to us, but no longer does so, now that we have transgressed the limit of creation, and changed our condition, and our nature is altered. But the fire is not changed in its nature, nor altered from its creation. Therefore it now has power over us; and when we come near it, it scorches our flesh.\""]],"45":[[1,"Then Adawm rose and prayed to Aluahim, saying, \"See, this fire has separated us from the cave in which You have commanded us to live; but now, behold, we cannot go into it.\""],[2,"Then Aluahim heard Adawm, and sent him His Word, that said: -"],[3,"\"O Adawm, see this fire! How different the flame and heat thereof are from the garden of delights and the good things in it!"],[4,"When you were under My control, all creatures yielded to you; but after you have transgressed My mitsvah, they all rise over you.\""],[5,"Aluahim said again to him, \"See, O Adawm, how Satan has exalted you! He has deprived you of the Aluahim, and of an exalted state like Me, and has not kept his word to you; but has, after all, become your enemy. He is the one who made this fire in which he meant to burn you and Ḥawwah."],[6,"Why, O Adawm, has he not kept his agreement with you, not even one day; but has deprived you of the esteem that was on you - when you yielded to his command?"],[7,"Do you think, Adawm, that he loved you when he made this agreement with you? Or that he loved you and wished to raise you on high?"],[8,"But no, Adawm, he did not do all that out of love to you; but he wished to make you come out of light into darkness; and from an exalted state to degradation; from esteem to abasement; from joy to sorrow; and from rest to fasting and fainting.\""],[9,"Aluahim also said to Adawm, \"See this fire kindled by Satan around your cave; see this wonder that surrounds you; and know that it will encompass about both you and your descendants, when you obey his command; that he will plague you with fire; and that you will go down into Sheol after you are dead."],[10,"Then you will see the burning of his fire, that will be burning around you and likewise your descendants. You will not be delivered from it until My coming; just like you cannot go into your cave right now because of the great fire around it; not until My Word comes and makes a way for you on the day My berith is fulfilled."],[11,"There is no way for you at present to come from this life to rest, not until My Word comes, who is My Word. Then He will make a way for you, and you shall have rest.\" Then Aluahim called with His Word to the fire that burned around the cave, that it split itself in half, until Adawm had gone through it. Then the fire parted itself by Aluahim's order, and a way was made for Adawm."],[12,"And Aluahim withdrew His Word from Adawm. Reference: Exodus 14:21,22 and Yahusha 3:15-17"]],"46":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah began again to come into the cave. And when they came to the way between the fire, Satan blew into the fire like a whirlwind, and caused the burning coal-fire to cover Adawm and Ḥawwah; so that their bodies were singed; and the coal-fire scorched them."],[2,"And from the burning of the fire Adawm and Ḥawwah screamed, and said, \"O Yahuah, save us! Leave us not to be consumed and plagued by this burning fire; neither require us for having transgressed Your mitsvah.\""],[3,"Then Aluahim looked at their bodies, on which Satan had caused fire to burn, and Aluahim sent His mal'ak that stayed the burning fire. But the wounds remained on their bodies."],[4,"And Aluahim said to Adawm, \"See Satan's love for you, who pretended to give you the Aluahim and greatness; and, behold, he burns you with fire, and seeks to destroy you from off the earth."],[5,"Then look at Me, O Adawm; I created you, and how many times have I delivered you out of his hand? If not, wouldn't he have destroyed you?\" 6 Aluahim said again to Ḥawwah, \"What is that he promised you in the garden, saying, 'As soon as you eat from the tree, your eyes will be opened, and you shall become like Aluahims, knowing good and evil.' But look! He has burnt your bodies with fire, and has made you taste the taste of fire, for the taste of the garden; and has made you see the burning of fire, and the evil of it, and the power it has over you."],[7,"Your eyes have seen the good he has taken from you, and in truth he has opened your eyes; and you have seen the garden in which you were with Me, and you have also seen the evil that has come over you from Satan. But as to the Aluahim he cannot give it to you, neither fulfil his speech to you. No, he was bitter against you and your descendants, that will come after you.\""],[8,"And Aluahim withdrew His Word form them. At this time, the garments that Yahuah had given them in Genesis 3:21 were burned off so that Adawm and Ḥawwah were again naked. Reference"]],"47":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah came into the cave, yet trembling at the fire that had scorched their bodies. So Adawm said to Ḥawwah: -"],[2,"\"Look, the fire has burnt our flesh in this world; but how will it be when we are dead, and Satan shall punish our nepheshoth? Is not our deliverance long and far off, unless Aluahim come, and in mercy to us fulfil His promise?\""],[3,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah passed into the cave, berakah themselves for coming into it once more. For it was in their thoughts, that they never should enter it, when they saw the fire around it."],[4,"But as the sun was setting the fire was still burning and nearing Adawm and Ḥawwah in the cave, so that they could not sleep in it. After the sun had set, they went out of it. This was the forty-seventh day after they came out of the garden."],[5,"Adawm and Ḥawwah then came under the top of hill by the garden to sleep, as they were accustomed."],[6,"And they stood and prayed Aluahim to forgive them their sins, and then fell asleep under the summit of the mountain."],[7,"But Satan, the hater of all good, thought within himself: \"Whereas Aluahim has promised yasha to Adawm by berith, and that He would deliver him out of all the hardships that have befallen him - but has not promised me by berith, and will not deliver me out of my hardships; no, since He has promised him that He should make him and his descendants live in the kingdom in which I once was - I will kill Adawm."],[8,"The earth shall be rid of him; and shall be left to me alone; so that when he is dead he may not have any descendants left to inherit the kingdom that shall remain my own realm; Aluahim will then be wanting me, and He will restore it to me and my hosts.\""]],"48":[[1,"After this Satan called to his hosts, all of which came to him, and said to him: -"],[2,"\"O, our Yahuah, what will you do?\""],[3,"He then said to them, \"You know that this Adawm, whom Aluahim created out of the dust, is the one who has taken our kingdom, come, let us gather together and kill him; or hurl a rock at him and at Ḥawwah, and crush them under it.\""],[4,"When Satan's hosts heard these words, they came to the part of the mountain where Adawm and Ḥawwah were asleep."],[5,"Then Satan and his host took a huge rock, broad and even, and without blemish, thinking within himself, \"If there should be a hole in the rock, when it fell on them, the hole in the rock might come over them, and so they would escape and not die.\""],[6,"He then said to his hosts, \"Take up this stone, and throw it flat on them, so that it doesn't roll off them to somewhere else. And when you have hurled it, get away from there quickly.\""],[7,"And they did as he told them. But as the rock fell down from the mountain toward Adawm and Ḥawwah, Aluahim commanded the rock to become a dome over them, that did them no harm. And so it was by Aluahim's order."],[8,"But when the rock fell, the whole earth quaked with it, and was shaken from the size of the rock."],[9,"And as it quaked and shook, Adawm and Ḥawwah awoke from sleep, and found themselves under a dome of rock. But they didn't know what had happened; because when the fell asleep they were under the sky, and not under a dome; and when they saw it, they were afraid."],[10,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Wherefore has the mountain bent itself, and the earth quaked and shaken on our account? And why has this rock spread itself over us like a tent?"],[11,"Does Aluahim intend to plague us and to shut us up in this prison? Or will He close the earth over us?"],[12,"He is angry with us for our having come out of the cave, without His order; and for our having done so of our own accord, without consulting Him, when we left the cave and came to this place.\""],[13,"Then Ḥawwah said, \"If, indeed, the earth quaked for our sake, and this rock forms a tent over us because of our transgression, then we will be sorry, O Adawm, because our punishment will be long."],[14,"But get up and pray to Aluahim to let us know concerning this, and what this rock is that is spread over us like a tent.\""],[15,"Then Adawm stood up and prayed before Yahuah, to let him know what had brought about this difficult time. And Adawm stood praying like that until the morning. The word \"dome\" is used here but the text does not specifically suggest that the covering was round only that it covered them on all sides, however a dome is the most likely shape that would have be able to withstand the impact with the ground. From verse"]],"49":[[1,"Then the Word of Aluahim came and said: -"],[2,"\"O Adawm, who counselled you, when you came out of the cave, to come to this place?\""],[3,"And Adawm said to Aluahim, \"O Yahuah, we came to this place because of the heat of the fire, that came over us inside the cave.\""],[4,"Then Yahuah Aluahim said to Adawm, \"O Adawm, you dread the heat of fire for one night, but how will it be when you live in Sheol?"],[5,"Yet, O Adawm, don't be afraid, and don't believe that I have placed this dome of rock over you to plague you with it."],[6,"It came from Satan, who had promised you the Aluahim and Greatness. It is he who threw down this rock to kill you under it, and Ḥawwah with you, and thus to prevent you from living on the earth."],[7,"But, in mercy for you, just as that rock was falling down on you, I commanded it to form an dome over you; and the rock under you to lower itself."],[8,"And this sign, O Adawm, will happen to Me at My coming on earth: Satan will raise the people of the Yahuḏim to put Me to death; and they will lay Me in a rock, and seal a large stone over Me, and I shall remain within that rock three days and three nights."],[9,"But on the third day I shall rise again, and it shall be yasha to you, O Adawm, and to your descendants, to believe in Me. But, O Adawm, I will not bring you from under this rock until three days and three nights have passed.\""],[10,"And Aluahim withdrew His Word from Adawm."],[11,"But Adawm and Ḥawwah lived under the rock three days and three nights, as Aluahim had told them."],[12,"And Aluahim did so to them because they had left their cave and had come to this same place without Aluahim's order."],[13,"But, after three days and three nights, Aluahim created an opening in the dome of rock and allowed them to get out from under it. Their flesh was dried up, and their eyes and hearts were troubled from crying and sorrow."]],"50":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah went forth and came into the Cave of Treasures, and they stood praying in it the whole of that day, until the evening."],[2,"And this took place at the end of the fifty days after they had left the garden."],[3,"But Adawm and Ḥawwah rose again and prayed to Aluahim in the cave the whole of that night, and begged for mercy from Him."],[4,"And when the day dawned, Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Come! Let us go and do some work for our bodies.\""],[5,"So they went out of the cave, and came to the northern border of the garden, and they looked for something to cover their bodies with. But they found nothing, and knew not how to do the work. Yet their bodies were stained, and they were speechless from cold and heat."],[6,"Then Adawm stood and asked Aluahim to show him something with which to cover their bodies."],[7,"Then came the Word of Aluahim and said to him, \"O Adawm, take Ḥawwah and come to the seashore where you fasted before. There you will find skins of sheep that were left after lions ate the carcasses. Take them and make garments for yourselves, and clothe yourselves with them."]],"51":[[1,"When Adawm heard these words from Aluahim, he took Ḥawwah and went from the northern end of the garden to the south of it, by the river of water where they once fasted."],[2,"But as they were going on their way, and before they got there, Satan, the wicked one, had heard the Word of Aluahim communing with Adawm respecting his covering."],[3,"It grieved him, and he hastened to the place where the sheep-skins were, with the intention of taking them and throwing them into the sea, or of burning them with fire, so that Adawm and Ḥawwah would not find them."],[4,"But as he was about to take them, the Word of Aluahim came from shamayim, and bound him by the side of those skins until Adawm and Ḥawwah came near him. But as they got closer to him they were afraid of him, and of his hideous look."],[5,"Then came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm and Ḥawwah, and said to them, \"This is he who was hidden in the serpent, and who deceived you, and stripped you of the garment of light and esteem in which you were."],[6,"This is he who promised you Greatness and Aluahim. Where, then, is the beauty that was on him? Where is his Aluahim? Where is his light? Where is the esteem that rested on him?"],[7,"Now his figure is hideous; he is become abominable among mal'akim; and he has come to be called Satan."],[8,"O Adawm, he wished to take from you this earthly garment of sheep-skins, and to destroy it, and not let you be covered with it."],[9,"What, then, is his beauty that you should have followed him? And what have you gained by obeying him? See his evil works and then look at Me; at Me, your Creator, and at the good deeds I do you."],[10,"See, I bound him until you came and saw him and beheld his weakness, that no power is left with him.\""],[11,"And Aluahim released him from his bonds."]],"52":[[1,"After this Adawm and Ḥawwah said no more, but cried before Aluahim on account of their creation, and of their bodies that required an earthly covering."],[2,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"O Ḥawwah, this is the skin of beasts with which we shall be covered, but when we put it on, behold, we shall be wearing a token of death on our bodies. Just as the owners of these skins have died and have wasted away, so also shall we die and pass away.\""],[3,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah took the skins, and went back to the Cave of Treasures; and when in it, they stood and prayed as they were accustomed."],[4,"And they thought how they could make garments of those skins; for they had no skill for it."],[5,"Then Aluahim sent to them His mal'ak to show them how to work it out. And the mal'ak said to Adawm, \"Go forth, and bring some palm-thorns.\" Then Adawm went out, and brought some, as the mal'ak had commanded him."],[6,"Then the mal'ak began before them to work out the skins, after the manner of one who prepares a shirt. And he took the thorns and stuck them into the skins, before their eyes."],[7,"Then the mal'ak again stood up and prayed Aluahim that the thorns in those skins should be hidden, so as to be, as it were, sewn with one thread."],[8,"And so it was, by Aluahim's order; they became garments for Adawm and Ḥawwah, and He clothed them therewith."],[9,"From that time the nakedness of their bodies was covered from the sight of each other's eyes."],[10,"And this happened at the end of the fifty-first day."],[11,"Then when Adawm's and Ḥawwah's bodies were covered, they stood and prayed, and sought mercy of Yahuah, and forgiveness, and gave Him thanks for that He had had mercy on them, and had covered their nakedness. And they ceased not from prayer the whole of that night."],[12,"Then when the morning dawned at the rising of the sun, they said their prayers after their custom; and then went out of the cave."],[13,"And Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Since we don't know what there is to the west of this cave, let us go out and see it today.\" Then they came forth and went toward the western border."]],"53":[[1,"They were not very far from the cave, when Satan came towards them, and hid himself between them and the cave, under the form of two ravenous lions three days without food, that came towards Adawm and Ḥawwah, as if to break them in pieces and devour them."],[2,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah cried, and prayed Aluahim to deliver them from their paws."],[3,"Then the Word of Aluahim came to them, and drove away the lions from them."],[4,"And Aluahim said to Adawm, \"O Adawm, what do you seek on the western border? And why have you left of thine own accord the eastern border, in which was your living place?"],[5,"Now then, turn back to your cave, and remain in it, so that Satan won't deceive you or work his purpose over you."],[6,"For in this western border, O Adawm, there will go from you a descendant, that shall replenish it; and that will defile themselves with their sins, and with their yielding to the commands of Satan, and by following his works. 7 Therefore will I bring over them the waters of a flood, and overwhelm them all. But I will deliver what is left of the righteous among them; and I will bring them to a distant land, and the land in which you live now shall remain desolate and without one inhabitant in it."],[8,"After Aluahim had thus spoken to them, they went back to the Cave of Treasures. But their flesh was dried up, and they were weak from fasting and praying, and from the sorrow they felt at having trespassed against Aluahim."]],"54":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah stood up in the cave and prayed the whole of that night until the morning dawned. And when the sun was risen they both went out of the cave; their heads were wandering from heaviness of sorrow and they didn't know where they were going."],[2,"And they walked in that condition to the southern border of the garden. And they began to go up that border until they came to the eastern border beyond which there was no more land. 3 And the cherub who guarded the garden was standing at the western gate, and guarding it against Adawm and Ḥawwah, lest they should suddenly come into the garden. And the cherub turned around, as if to put them to death; according to the mitsvah Aluahim had given him. 4 When Adawm and Ḥawwah came to the eastern border of the garden - thinking in their hearts that the cherub was not watching - as they were standing by the gate as if wishing to go in, suddenly came the cherub with a flashing sword of fire in his hand; and when he saw them, he went forth to kill them. For he was afraid that Aluahim would destroy him if they went into the garden without His order."],[5,"And the sword of the cherub seemed to shoot flames a distance away from it. But when he raised it over Adawm and Ḥawwah, the flame of the sword did not flash forth."],[6,"Therefore the cherub thought that Aluahim was favorable to them, and was bringing them back into the garden. And the cherub stood wondering."],[7,"He could not go up to Shamayim to determine Aluahim's order regarding their getting into the garden; he therefore continued to stand by them, unable as he was to part from them; for he was afraid that if they should enter the garden without permission, Aluahim would destroy him."],[8,"When Adawm and Ḥawwah saw the cherub coming towards them with a flaming sword of fire in his hand, they fell on their faces from fear, and were as dead."],[9,"At that time the shamayim and the earth shook; and another cherubim came down from shamayim to the cherub who guarded the garden, and saw him amazed and silent."],[10,"Then, again, other mal'akim came down close to the place where Adawm and Ḥawwah were. They were divided between joy and sorrow."],[11,"They were glad, because they thought that Aluahim was favorable to Adawm, and wished him to return to the garden; and wished to restore him to the gladness he once enjoyed."],[12,"But they sorrowed over Adawm, because he was fallen like a dead man, he and Ḥawwah; and they said in their thoughts, \"Adawm has not died in this place; but Aluahim has put him to death, for his having come to this place, and wishing to get into the garden without His permission.\""]],"55":[[1,"Then came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm and Ḥawwah, and raised them from their dead state, saying to them, \"Why did you come up here? Do you intend to go into the garden, from which I brought you out? It cannot be today; but only when the berith I have made with you is fulfilled.\""],[2,"Then Adawm, when he heard the Word of Aluahim, and the fluttering of the mal'akim whom he did not see, but only heard the sound of them with his ears, he and Ḥawwah cried, and said to the mal'akim: -"],[3,"\"O Ruchot, who wait on Aluahim, look at me, and at my being unable to see you! For when I was in my former bright nature, then I could see you. I sang praises as you do; and my heart was far above you."],[4,"But now, that I have transgressed, that bright nature is gone from me, and I am come to this miserable state. And now I have come to this, that I cannot see you, and you do not serve me like you used to do. For I have become animal flesh."],[5,"Yet now, O mal'akim of Aluahim, ask Aluahim with me, to restore me to that wherein I was formerly; to rescue me from this misery, and to remove from me the sentence of death He passed on me, for having trespassed against Him.\""],[6,"Then, when the mal'akim heard these words, they all grieved over him; and cursed Satan who had misled Adawm, until he came from the garden to misery; from life to death; from shalom to trouble; and from gladness to a strange land."],[7,"Then the mal'akim said to Adawm, \"You obeyed Satan, and ignored the Word of Aluahim who created you; and you believed that Satan would fulfil all he had promised you."],[8,"But now, O Adawm, we will make known to you, what came over us though him, before his fall from shamayim."],[9,"He gathered together his hosts, and deceived them, promising to give them a great kingdom, a Mighty-like nature; and other promises he made them. 10 His hosts believed that his word was true, so they yielded to him, and renounced the esteem of Aluahim."],[11,"He then sent for us - according to the orders in which we were - to come under his command, and to accept his vein promise. But we would not, and we did not take his advice."],[12,"Then after he had fought with Aluahim, and had dealt forwardly with Him, he gathered together his hosts, and made war with us. And if it had not been for Aluahim's strength that was with us, we could not have prevailed against him to hurl him from shamayim."],[13,"But when he fell from among us, there was great joy in shamayim, because of his going down from us. For if he had remained in shamayim, nothing, not even one mal'ak would have remained in it."],[14,"But Aluahim in His mercy, drove him from among us to this dark earth; for he had become darkness itself and a worker of unrighteousness."],[15,"And he has continued, O Adawm, to make war against you, until he tricked you and made you come out of the garden, to this strange land, where all these trials have come to you. And death, which Aluahim brought to him, he has also brought to you, O Adawm, because you obeyed him, and trespassed against Aluahim.\""],[16,"Then all the mal'akim rejoiced and praised Aluahim, and asked Him not to destroy Adawm this time, for his having sought to enter the garden; but to bear with him until the fulfillment of the promise; and to help him in this world until he was free from Satan's hand."]],"56":[[1,"Then came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm, and said to him: -"],[2,"\"O Adawm, look at that garden of joy and at this earth of toil, and behold the garden is full of mal'akim, but look at yourself alone on this earth with Satan whom you obeyed."],[3,"Yet, if you had submitted, and been obedient to Me, and had kept My Word, you would be with My mal'akim in My garden."],[4,"But when you transgressed and obeyed Satan, you became his guests among his mal'akim, that are full of wickedness; and you came to this earth, that brings forth to you thorns and thistles."],[5,"O Adawm, ask him who deceived you, to give you the Mighty-like nature he promised you, or to make you a garden as I had made for you; or to fill you with that same bright nature with which I had filled you."],[6,"Ask him to make you a body like the one I made you, or to give you a day of rest as I gave you; or to create within you a reasonable nephesh, as I created for you; or to take you from here to some other earth than this one which I gave you. But, O Adawm, he will not fulfil even one of the things he told you."],[7,"Acknowledge, then, My chen towards you, and My mercy on you, My creature; that I have not avenged you for your transgression against Me, but in My pity for you I have promised you that at the end of the great five and a half days I will come and save you.\""],[8,"Then Aluahim said again to Adawm and Ḥawwah, \"Get up, go down from here, before the cherub with a sword of fire in his hand destroys you.\""],[9,"But Adawm's heart was comforted by Aluahim's words to him, and he worshipped before Him."],[10,"And Aluahim commanded His mal'akim to escort Adawm and Ḥawwah to the cave with joy, instead of the fear that had come over them."],[11,"Then the mal'akim took up Adawm and Ḥawwah, and brought them down from the mountain by the garden, with songs and psalms, until they arrived at the cave. There the mal'akim began to comfort and to strengthen them, and then departed from them towards shamayim, to their Creator, who had sent them."],[12,"But after the mal'akim had departed from Adawm and Ḥawwah, Satan came with shamefacedness, and stood at the entrance of the cave in which were Adawm and Ḥawwah. He then called to Adawm, and said, \"O Adawm, come, let me speak to you.\""],[13,"Then Adawm came out of the cave, thinking he was one of Aluahim's mal'akim that was come to give him some good counsel."]],"57":[[1,"But when Adawm came out and saw his hideous figure, he was afraid of him, and said to him, \"Who are you?\""],[2,"Then Satan answered and said to him, \"It is I, who hid myself within the serpent, and who spoke to Ḥawwah, and who enticed her until she obeyed my command. I am he who sent her, using my deceitful speech, to deceive you, until you both ate of the fruit of the tree and abandoned the command of Aluahim.\""],[3,"But when Adawm heard these words from him, he said to him, \"Can you make me a garden as Aluahim made for me? Or can you clothe me in the same bright nature in which Aluahim had clothed me?"],[4,"Where is the Mighty-like nature you promised to give me? Where is that slick speech of yours that you had with us at first, when we were in the garden?\""],[5,"Then Satan said to Adawm, \"Do you think that when I have promised one something that I would actually deliver it to him or fulfil my word? Of course not. For I myself have never even thought of obtaining what I promised."],[6,"Therefore I fell, and I made you fall by that for which I myself fell; and with you also, whosoever accepts my counsel, falls thereby."],[7,"But now, O Adawm, because you fell you are under my rule, and I am king over you; because you have obeyed me and have transgressed against your Aluahim. Neither will there be any deliverance from my hands until the day promised you by your Aluahim.\""],[8,"Again he said, \"Because we do not know the day agreed on with you by your Aluahim, nor the hour in which you shall be delivered, for that reason we will multiply war and murder on you and your descendants after you."],[9,"This is our will and our good pleasure, that we may not leave one of the sons of men to inherit our orders in shamayim."],[10,"For as to our home, O Adawm, it is in burning fire; and we will not stop our evil doing, no, not one day nor one hour. And I, O Adawm, shall set you on fire when you come into the cave to live there.\""],[11,"When Adawm heard these words he cried and mourned, and said to Ḥawwah, \"Hear what he said; that he won't fulfil any of what he told you in the garden. Did he really then become king over us?"],[12,"But we will ask Aluahim, who created us, to deliver us out of his hands.\""]],"58":[[1,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah spread their hands before Aluahim, praying and begging Him to drive Satan away from them so that he can't harm them or force them to deny Aluahim."],[2,"Then Aluahim sent to them at once, His mal'ak, who drove away Satan from them. This happened about sunset, on the fifty-third day after they had come out of the garden."],[3,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah went into the cave, and stood up and turned their faces to the ground, to pray to Aluahim."],[4,"But before they prayed Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Look, you have seen what temptations have befallen us in this land. Come, let us get up, and ask Aluahim to forgive us the sins we have committed; and we will not come out until the end of the day next to the fortieth. And if we die in here, He will save us.\""],[5,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah got up, and joined together in entreating Aluahim."],[6,"They continued praying like this in the cave; neither did they come out of it, by night or by day, until their prayers went up out of their mouths, like a flame of fire."]],"59":[[1,"But Satan, the hater of all good, did not allow them to finish their prayers. For he called to his hosts, and they came, all of them. Then he said to them, \"Since Adawm and Ḥawwah, whom we deceived, have agreed together to pray to Aluahim night and day, and to beg Him to deliver them, and since they will not come out of the cave until the end of the fortieth day."],[2,"And since they will continue their prayers as they have both agreed to do, that He will deliver them out of our hands, and restore them to their former state, see what we shall do to them.\" And his hosts said to him, \"Power is thine, O our Yahuah, to do what you list.\""],[3,"Then Satan, great in wickedness, took his hosts and came into the cave, in the thirtieth night of the forty days and one; and he beat Adawm and Ḥawwah, until he left them dead."],[4,"Then came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm and Ḥawwah, who raised them from their suffering, and Aluahim said to Adawm, \"Be strong, and be not afraid of him who has just come to you.\""],[5,"But Adawm cried and said, \"Where were you, O my Aluahim, that they should punish me with such blows, and that this suffering should come over us; over me and over Ḥawwah, Your handmaiden?\""],[6,"Then Aluahim said to him, \"O Adawm, see, he is Yahuah and master of all you have, he who said, he would give you Aluahim. Where is this love for you? And where is the gift he promised?"],[7,"Did it please him just once, O Adawm, to come to you, comfort you, strengthen you, rejoice with you, or send his hosts to protect you; because you have obeyed him, and have yielded to his counsel; and have followed his mitsvah and transgressed Mine?\""],[8,"Then Adawm cried before Yahuah, and said, \"O Yahuah because I transgressed a little, You have severely punished me in return for it, I ask You to deliver me out of his hands; or else have pity on me, and take my nephesh out of my body now in this strange land.\""],[9,"Then Aluahim said to Adawm, \"If only there had been this sighing and praying before, before you transgressed! Then would you have rest from the trouble in which you are now.\""],[10,"But Aluahim had patience with Adawm, and let him and Ḥawwah remain in the cave until they had fulfilled the forty days."],[11,"But as to Adawm and Ḥawwah, their strength and flesh withered from fasting and praying, from hunger and thirst; for they had not tasted either food or drink since they left the garden; nor were the functions of their bodies yet settled; and they had no strength left to continue in prayer from hunger, until the end of the next day to the fortieth. They were fallen down in the cave; yet what speech escaped from their mouths, was only in praises."]],"60":[[1,"Then on the eighty-ninth day, Satan came to the cave, clad in a garment of light, and girt about with a bright girdle."],[2,"In his hands was a staff of light, and he looked most awful; but his face was pleasant and his speech was sweet."],[3,"He thus transformed himself in order to deceive Adawm and Ḥawwah, and to make them come out of the cave, before they had fulfilled the forty days."],[4,"For he said within himself, \"Now that when they had fulfilled the forty days' fasting and praying, Aluahim would restore them to their former state; but if He did not do so, He would still be favorable to them; and even if He had not mercy on them, would He yet give them something from the garden to comfort them; as already twice before.\""],[5,"Then Satan drew near the cave in this fair appearance, and said: -"],[6,"\"O Adawm, get up, stand up, you and Ḥawwah, and come along with me, to a good land; and don't be afraid. I am flesh and bones like you; and at first I was a creature that Aluahim created."],[7,"And it was so, that when He had created me, He placed me in a garden in the north, on the border of the world."],[8,"And He said to me, 'Stay here!' And I remained there according to His Word, neither did I transgress His mitsvah."],[9,"Then He made a slumber to come over me, and He brought you, O Adawm, out of my side, but did not make you stay with me."],[10,"But Aluahim took you in His Mighty-like hand, and placed you in a garden to the eastward."],[11,"Then I worried about you, for that while Aluahim had taken you out of my side, He had not let you stay with me."],[12,"But Aluahim said to me: 'Do not worry about Adawm, whom I brought out of your side; no harm will come to him."],[13,"For now I have brought out of his side a help-meet for him; and I have given him joy by so doing.' \""],[14,"Then Satan said again, \"I did not know how it is you are in this cave, nor anything about this trial that has come over you - until Aluahim said to me, 'Behold, Adawm has transgressed, he whom I had taken out of your side, and Ḥawwah also, whom I took out of his side; and I have driven them out of the garden; I have made them live in a land of sorrow and misery, because they transgressed against Me, and have obeyed Satan. And look, they are in suffering until this day, the eightieth.' 15 Then Aluahim said to me, 'Get up, go to them, and make them come to your place, and suffer not that Satan come near them, and afflict them. For they are now in great misery; and lie helpless from hunger.'"],[16,"He further said to me, 'When you have taken them to yourself, give them to eat of the fruit of the Tree of Life, and give them to drink of the water of shalom; and clothe them in a garment of light, and restore them to their former state of chen, and leave them not in misery, for they came from you. But grieve not over them, nor repent of that which has come over them."],[17,"But when I heard this, I was sorry; and my heart could not patiently bear it for your sake, O my child."],[18,"But, O Adawm, when I heard the name of Satan, I was afraid, and I said within myself, I will not come out because he might trap me as he did my children, Adawm and Ḥawwah."],[19,"And I said, 'O Aluahim, when I go to my children, Satan will meet me in the way, and war against me, as he did against them.'"],[20,"Then Aluahim said to me, 'Fear not; when you find him, hit him with the staff that is in thine hand, and don't be afraid of him, for you are of old standing, and he shall not prevail against you.'"],[21,"Then I said, 'O my Yahuah, I am old, and cannot go. Send Your mal'akim to bring them.'"],[22,"But Aluahim said to me, 'Mal'akim, verily, are not like them; and they will not consent to come with them. But I have chosen you, because they are your offspring and are like you, and they will listen to what you say.'"],[23,"Aluahim said further to me, 'If you don't have enough strength to walk, I will send a cloud to carry you and set you down at the entrance of their cave; then the cloud will return and leave you there."],[24,"And if they will come with you, I will send a cloud to carry you and them.'"],[25,"Then He commanded a cloud, and it bear me up and brought me to you; and then went back."],[26,"And now, O my children, Adawm and Ḥawwah, look at my old gray hair and at my feeble state, and at my coming from that distant place. Come, come with me, to a place of rest.\""],[27,"Then he began to cry and to sob before Adawm and Ḥawwah, and his tears poured on the ground like water."],[28,"And when Adawm and Ḥawwah raised their eyes and saw his beard, and heard his sweet talk, their hearts softened towards him; they obeyed him, for they believed he was true."],[29,"And it seemed to them that they were really his offspring, when they saw that his face was like their own; and they trusted him. The existence of the two words helpmeet and helpmate, meaning exactly the same thing, is a comedy of errors. Aluahim's promise to Adawm, as rendered in the King James version of the Bible, was to give him an help meet for him (that is, a helper fit for him). In the 17th century the two words help and meet in this passage were mistaken for one word, applying to Ḥawwah, and thus helpmeet came to mean a wife. Then in the 18th century, in a misguided attempt to make sense of the word, the spelling helpmate was introduced. Both errors are now beyond recall, and both spellings are acceptable."]],"61":[[1,"Then he took Adawm and Ḥawwah by the hand, and began to bring them out of the cave."],[2,"But when they had come a little ways out of it, Aluahim knew that Satan had overcome them, and had brought them out before the forty days were ended, to take them to some distant place, and to destroy them."],[3,"Then the Word of Yahuah Aluahim again came and cursed Satan, and drove him away from them."],[4,"And Aluahim began to speak to Adawm and Ḥawwah, saying to them, \"What made you come out of the cave, to this place?\""],[5,"Then Adawm said to Aluahim, \"Did you create a man before us? For when we were in the cave there suddenly came to us a friendly old man who said to us, 'I am a mal'ak from Aluahim to you, to bring you back to some place of rest.'"],[6,"And we believed, O Aluahim, that he was a mal'ak from you; and we came out with him; and knew not where we should go with him.\""],[7,"Then Aluahim said to Adawm, \"See, that is the father of evil arts, who brought you and Ḥawwah out of the Garden of Delights. And now, indeed, when he saw that you and Ḥawwah both joined together in fasting and praying, and that you came not out of the cave before the end of the forty days, he wished to make your purpose vein, to break your mutual bond; to cut off all hope from you, and to drive you to some place where he might destroy you."],[8,"Because he couldn't do anything to you unless he showed himself in the likeness of you."],[9,"Therefore he came to you with a face like your own, and began to give you tokens as if they were all true."],[10,"But because I am merciful and am favorable to you, I did not allow him to destroy you; instead I drove him away from you."],[11,"Now, therefore, O Adawm, take Ḥawwah, and return to your cave, and remain in it until the morning after the fortieth day. And when you come out, go towards the eastern gate of the garden.\""],[12,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah worshipped Aluahim, and praised and baruk Him for the deliverance that had come to them from Him. And they returned towards the cave. This happened in the evening of the thirty-ninth day."],[13,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah stood up and with a fiery passion, prayed to Aluahim, to give them strength; for they had become weak because of hunger and thirst and prayer. But they watched the whole of that night praying, until morning."],[14,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Get up, let us go towards the eastern gate of the garden as Aluahim told us.\""],[15,"And they said their prayers as they were accustomed to do every day; and they left the cave to go near to the eastern gate of the garden."],[16,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah stood up and prayed, and appealed to Aluahim to strengthen them, and to send them something to satisfy their hunger."],[17,"But after they finished their prayers, they were too weak to move."],[18,"Then came the Word of Aluahim again, and said to them, \"O Adawm, get up, go and bring the two figs here.\""],[19,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah got up, and went until they came near to the cave."]],"62":[[1,"But Satan the wicked was envious, because of the consolation Aluahim had given them."],[2,"So he prevented them, and went into the cave and took the two figs, and buried them outside the cave, so that Adawm and Ḥawwah should not find them. He also had in his thoughts to destroy them."],[3,"But by Aluahim's mercy, as soon as those two figs were in the ground, Aluahim defeated Satan's counsel regarding them; and made them into two fruit trees, that overshadowed the cave. For Satan had buried them on the eastern side of it."],[4,"Then when the two trees were grown, and were covered with fruit, Satan grieved and mourned, and said, \"It would have been better to have left those figs where they were; for now, behold, they have become two fruit trees, whereof Adawm will eat all the days of his life. Whereas I had in mind, when I buried them, to destroy them entirely, and to hide them forever."],[5,"But Aluahim has overturned my counsel; and would not that this qadash (Set Apart) fruit should perish; and He has made plain my intention, and has defeated the counsel I had formed against His servants.\""],[6,"Then Satan went away ashamed because he hadn't thought his plans all the way through."]],"63":[[1,"But Adawm and Ḥawwah, as they got closer to the cave, saw two fig trees, covered with fruit, and overshadowing the cave."],[2,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"It seems to me that we have gone the wrong way. When did these two trees grow here? It seems to me that the enemy wishes to lead us the wrong way. Do you suppose that there is another cave besides this one in the earth?"],[3,"Yet, O Ḥawwah, let us go into the cave, and find in it the two figs; for this is our cave, in which we were. But if we should not find the two figs in it, then it cannot be our cave.\""],[4,"They went then into the cave, and looked into the four corners of it, but found not the two figs."],[5,"And Adawm cried and said to Ḥawwah, \"Did we go to the wrong cave, then, O Ḥawwah? It seems to me these two fig trees are the two figs that were in the cave.\" And Ḥawwah said, \"I, for my part, do not know.\""],[6,"Then Adawm stood up and prayed and said, \"O Aluahim, You commanded us to come back to the cave, to take the two figs, and then to return to you."],[7,"But now, we have not found them. O Aluahim, have you taken them, and sown these two trees, or have we gone astray in the earth; or has the enemy deceived us? If it be real, then, O Aluahim, reveal to us the secret of these two trees and of the two figs.\""],[8,"Then came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm, and said to him, \"O Adawm, when I sent you to fetch the figs, Satan went before you to the cave, took the figs, and buried them outside, eastward of the cave, thinking to destroy them; and not sowing them with good intent."],[9,"Not for his mere sake, then, have these trees grown up at once; but I had mercy on you and I commanded them to grow. And they grew to be two large trees, that you be overshadowed by their branches, and find rest; and that I made you see My power and My marvelous works."],[10,"And, also, to show you Satan's meanness, and his evil works, for ever since you came out of the garden, he has not ceased, no, not one day, from doing you some harm. But I have not given him power over you.\""],[11,"And Aluahim said, \"From now on, O Adawm, rejoice on account of the trees, you and Ḥawwah; and rest under them when you feel weary. But do not eat any of their fruit or come near them.\""],[12,"Then Adawm cried, and said, \"O Aluahim, will You again kill us, or will You drive us away from before Your face, and cut our life from off the face of the earth?"],[13,"O Aluahim, I beg you, if You know that there be in these trees either death or some other evil, as at the first time, root them up from near our cave, and with them; and leave us to die of the heat, of hunger and of thirst."],[14,"For we know Your marvelous works, O Aluahim, that they are great, and that by Your power You can bring one thing out of another, without one's wish. For Your power can make rocks to become trees, and trees to become rocks.\""]],"64":[[1,"Then Aluahim looked at Adawm and at his strength of mind, at his endurance of hunger and thirst, and of the heat. And He changed the two fig trees into two figs, as they were at first, and then said to Adawm and to Ḥawwah, \"Each of you may take one fig.\" And they took them, as Yahuah commanded them."],[2,"And He said to them, \"You must now go into the cave and eat the figs, and satisfy your hunger, or else you will die.\""],[3,"So, as Aluahim commanded them, they went into the cave about sunset. And Adawm and Ḥawwah stood up and prayed during the setting sun."],[4,"Then they sat down to eat the figs; but they knew not how to eat them; for they were not accustomed to eat earthly food. They were afraid that if they ate, their stomach would be burdened and their flesh thickened, and their hearts would take to liking earthly food."],[5,"But while they were thus seated, Aluahim, out of pity for them, sent them His mal'ak, so they wouldn't perish of hunger and thirst."],[6,"And the mal'ak said to Adawm and Ḥawwah, \"Aluahim says to you that you do not have the strength that would be required to fast until death; eat, therefore, and strengthen your bodies; for you are now animal flesh and cannot subsist without food and drink.\""],[7,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah took the figs and began to eat of them. But Aluahim had put into them a mixture as of savory bread and blood."],[8,"Then the mal'ak went from Adawm and Ḥawwah, who ate of the figs until they had satisfied their hunger. Then they put aside what was left; but by the power of Aluahim, the figs became whole again, because Aluahim baruk them."],[9,"After this Adawm and Ḥawwah got up, and prayed with a joyful heart and renewed strength, and praised and rejoiced abundantly the whole of that night. And this was the end of the eighty-third day."]],"65":[[1,"And when it was day, they got up and prayed, after their custom, and then went out of the cave."],[2,"But they became sick from the food they had eaten because they were not used to it, so they went about in the cave saying to each other: -"],[3,"\"What has our eating caused to happen to us, that we should be in such pain? We are in misery, we shall die! It would have been better for us to have died keeping our bodies pure than to have eaten and defiled them with food.\""],[4,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"This pain did not come to us in the garden, neither did we eat such bad food there. Do you think, O Ḥawwah, that Aluahim will plague us through the food that is in us, or that our innards will come out; or that Aluahim means to kill us with this pain before He has fulfilled His promise to us?\""],[5,"Then Adawm besought Yahuah and said, \"O Yahuah, let us not perish through the food we have eaten. O Yahuah, don't punish us; but deal with us according to Your great mercy, and forsake us not until the day of the promise You have made us.\""],[6,"Then Aluahim looked at them, and then fitted them for eating food at once; as to this day; so that they should not perish."],[7,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah came back into the cave sorrowful and crying because of the alteration of their bodies. And they both knew from that hour that they were altered beings, that all hope of returning to the garden was now lost; and that they could not enter it."],[8,"For that now their bodies had strange functions; and all flesh that requires food and drink for its existence, cannot be in the garden."],[9,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Behold, our hope is now lost; and so is our trust to enter the garden. We no longer belong to the inhabitants of the garden; but from now on we are earthy and of the dust, and of the inhabitants of the earth. We shall not return to the garden, until the day in which Aluahim has promised to save us, and to bring us again into the garden, as He promised us.\""],[10,"Then they prayed to Aluahim that He would have mercy on them; after which, their mind was quieted, their hearts were broken, and their longing was cooled down; and they were like strangers on earth. That night Adawm and Ḥawwah spent in the cave, where they slept heavily by reason of the food they had eaten."]],"66":[[1,"When it was morning, the day after they had eaten food, Adawm and Ḥawwah prayed in the cave, and Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Look, we asked for food of Aluahim, and He gave it. But now let us also ask Him to give us a drink of water.\""],[2,"Then they got up, and went to the bank of the stream of water, that was on the south border of the garden, in which they had before thrown themselves. And they stood on the bank, and prayed to Aluahim that He would command them to drink of the water."],[3,"Then the Word of Aluahim came to Adawm, and said to him, \"O Adawm, your body has become brutish, and requires water to drink. Take some and drink it, you and Ḥawwah, then give thanks and praise.\""],[4,"Adawm and Ḥawwah then went down to the stream and drank from it, until their bodies felt refreshed. After having drunk, they praised Aluahim, and then returned to their cave, after their former custom. This happened at the end of eighty-three days."],[5,"Then on the eighty-fourth day, they took the two figs and hung them in the cave, together with the leaves thereof, to be to them a sign and a berakah from Aluahim. And they placed them there so that if their descendants came there, they would see the wonderful things Aluahim had done for them."],[6,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah again stood outside the cave, and asked Aluahim to show them some food with which they could nourish their bodies."],[7,"Then the Word of Aluahim came and said to him, \"O Adawm, go down to the westward of the cave until you come to a land of dark soil, and there you shall find food.\""],[8,"And Adawm obeyed the Word of Aluahim, took Ḥawwah, and went down to a land of dark soil, and found there wheat growing in the ear and ripe, and figs to eat; and Adawm rejoiced over it."],[9,"Then the Word of Aluahim came again to Adawm, and said to him, \"Take some of this wheat and make yourselves some bread with it, to nourish your body therewith.\" And Aluahim gave Adawm's heart wisdom, to work out the corn until it became bread."],[10,"Adawm accomplished all that, until he grew very faint and weary. He then returned to the cave; rejoicing at what he had learned of what is done with wheat, until it is made into bread for one's use. In this book, the terms 'corn' and 'wheat' are used interchangeably. The reference is possibly used to indicate a type of ancient grain resembling Mitsrite Corn also known as Durra. Durra is a wheat-like cereal grain frequently cultivated in dry regions such as Mitsrayim."]],"67":[[1,"When Adawm and Ḥawwah went down to the land of black mud and came near to the wheat Aluahim had showed them and saw that it was ripe and ready for reaping, they did not have a sickle to reap it with. So they readied themselves, and began to pull up the wheat by hand, until it was all done."],[2,"Then they heaped it into a pile; and, faint from heat and from thirst, they went under a shady tree, where the breeze fanned them to sleep."],[3,"But Satan saw what Adawm and Ḥawwah had done. And he called his hosts, and said to them, \"Since Aluahim has shown to Adawm and Ḥawwah all about this wheat, wherewith to strengthen their bodies - and, look, they have come and made a big pile of it, and faint from the toil are now asleep - come, let us set fire to this heap of corn, and burn it, and let us take that bottle of water that is by them, and empty it out, so that they may find nothing to drink, and we kill them with hunger and thirst."],[4,"Then, when they wake up from their sleep, and seek to return to the cave, we will come to them in the way, and will lead them astray; so that they die of hunger and thirst; when they may, perhaps, deny Aluahim, and He destroy them. So shall we be rid of them.\""],[5,"Then Satan and his hosts set the wheat on fire and burned it up."],[6,"But from the heat of the flame Adawm and Ḥawwah awoke from their sleep, and saw the wheat burning, and the bucket of water by them, poured out."],[7,"Then they cried and went back to the cave."],[8,"But as they were going up from below the mountain where they were, Satan and his hosts met them in the form of mal'akim, praising Aluahim."],[9,"Then Satan said to Adawm, \"O Adawm, why are you so pained with hunger and thirst? It seems to me that Satan has burnt up the wheat.\" And Adawm said to him, \"Yes.\""],[10,"Again Satan said to Adawm, \"Come back with us; we are mal'akim of Aluahim. Aluahim sent us to you, to show you another field of corn, better than that; and beyond it is a fountain of good water, and many trees, where you shall live near it, and work the corn field to better purpose than that which Satan has consumed.\""],[11,"Adawm thought that he was true, and that they were mal'akim who talked with him; and he went back with them."],[12,"Then Satan began to lead astray Adawm and Ḥawwah eight days, until they both fell down as if dead, from hunger, thirst, and faintness. Then he fled with his hosts, and left them."]],"68":[[1,"Then Aluahim looked at Adawm and Ḥawwah, and at what had come over them from Satan, and how he had made them perish."],[2,"Aluahim, therefore, sent His Word, and raised up Adawm and Ḥawwah from their state of death."],[3,"Then, Adawm, when he was raised, said, \"O Aluahim, You have burnt and taken from us the corn You have given us, and You have emptied out the bucket of water. And You have sent Your mal'akim, who have caused us to lose our way from the corn field. Will You make us perish? If this be from you, O Aluahim, then take away our nepheshoth; but punish us not.\""],[4,"Then Aluahim said to Adawm, \"I did not burn down the wheat, and I did not pour the water out of the bucket, and I did not send My mal'akim to lead you astray."],[5,"But it is Satan, your master who did it; he to whom you have subjected yourself; my mitsvah being meanwhile set aside. He it is, who burnt down the corn, and poured out the water, and who has led you astray; and all the promises he has made you were just a trick, a deception, and a lie."],[6,"But now, O Adawm, you shall acknowledge My good deeds done to you.\""],[7,"And Aluahim told His mal'akim to take Adawm and Ḥawwah, and to bear them up to the field of wheat, which they found as before, with the bucket full of water. 8 There they saw a tree, and found on it solid manna; and wondered at Aluahim's power. And the mal'akim commanded them to eat of the manna when they were hungry."],[9,"And Aluahim admonished Satan with a curse, not to come again, and destroy the field of corn."],[10,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah took of the corn, and made of it an offering, and took it and offered it up on the mountain, the place where they had offered up their first offering of blood."],[11,"And they offered this offering again on the mizbe'ach they had built at first. And they stood up and prayed, and besought Yahuah saying, \"Thus, O Aluahim, when we were in the garden, our praises went up to you, like this offering; and our innocence went up to you like incense. But now, O Aluahim, accept this offering from us, and don't turn us away, deprived of Your mercy.\""],[12,"Then Aluahim said to Adawm and Ḥawwah, \"Since you have made this offering and have offered it to Me, I shall make it My flesh, when I come down on earth to save you; and I shall cause it to be offered continually on an mizbe'ach, for forgiveness and for mercy, for those who partake of it duly.\""],[13,"And Aluahim sent a bright fire over the offering of Adawm and Ḥawwah, and filled it with brightness, chen, and light; and the Ruach HaQadash came down on that offering."],[14,"Then Aluahim commanded an mal'ak to take fire tongs, like a spoon, and with it to take an offering and bring it to Adawm and Ḥawwah. And the mal'ak did so, as Aluahim had commanded him, and offered it to them."],[15,"And the nepheshoth of Adawm and Ḥawwah were brightened, and their hearts were filled with joy and gladness and with the praises of Aluahim."],[16,"And Aluahim said to Adawm, \"This shall be to you a custom, to do so, when affliction and sorrow come over you. But your deliverance and your entrance in to the garden, shall not be until the days are fulfilled as agreed between you and Me; were it not so, I would, of My mercy and pity for you, bring you back to My garden and to My chen for the sake of the offering you have just made to My name.\""],[17,"Adawm rejoiced at these words which he heard from Aluahim; and he and Ḥawwah worshipped before the mizbe'ach, to which they bowed, and then went back to the Cave of Treasures."],[18,"And this took place at the end of the twelfth day after the eightieth day, from the time Adawm and Ḥawwah came out of the garden."],[19,"And they stood up the whole night praying until morning; and then went out of the cave."],[20,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, with joy of heart, because of the offering they had made to Aluahim, and that had been accepted of Him, \"Let us do this three times every week, on the fourth day Wednesday, on the preparation day Friday, and on the Shabbath Sunday, all the days of our life.\""],[21,"And as they agreed to these words between themselves, Aluahim was pleased with their thoughts, and with the resolution they had each taken with the other."],[22,"After this, came the Word of Aluahim to Adawm, and said, \"O Adawm, you have determined beforehand the days in which sufferings shall come over Me, when I am made flesh; for they are the fourth Wednesday, and the preparation day Friday."],[23,"But as to the first day, I created in it all things, and I raised the shamayim. And, again, through My rising again on this day, will I create joy, and raise them on high, who believe in Me; O Adawm, offer this offering, all the days of your life.\""],[24,"Then Aluahim withdrew His Word from Adawm."],[25,"But Adawm continued to offer this offering thus, every week three times, until the end of seven weeks. And on the first day, which is the fiftieth, Adawm made an offering as he was accustomed, and he and Ḥawwah took it and came to the mizbe'ach before Aluahim, as He had taught them."]],"69":[[1,"Then Satan, the hater of all good, envious of Adawm and of his offering through which he found chen with Aluahim, hastened and took a sharp stone from among the sharp iron stones; appeared in the form of a man, and went and stood by Adawm and Ḥawwah."],[2,"Adawm was then offering on the mizbe'ach, and had begun to pray, with his hands spread before Aluahim."],[3,"Then Satan hastened with the sharp iron stone he had with him, and with it pierced Adawm on the right side, from which flowed blood and water, then Adawm fell on the mizbe'ach like a corpse. And Satan fled."],[4,"Then Ḥawwah came, and took Adawm and placed him below the mizbe'ach. And there she stayed, crying over him; while a stream of blood flowed from Adawm's side over his offering."],[5,"But Aluahim looked at the death of Adawm. He then sent His Word, and raised him up and said to him, \"Fulfil your offering, for indeed, Adawm, it is worth much, and there is no shortcoming in it.\""],[6,"Aluahim said further to Adawm, \"Thus will it also happen to Me, on the earth, when I shall be pierced and blood and water shall flow from My side and run over My body, which is the true offering; and which shall be offered on the mizbe'ach as a perfect offering.\""],[7,"Then Aluahim commanded Adawm to finish his offering, and when he had ended it he worshipped before Aluahim, and praised Him for the signs He had showed him."],[8,"And Aluahim healed Adawm in one day, which is the end of the seven weeks; and that is the fiftieth day."],[9,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah returned from the mountain, and went into the Cave of Treasures, as they were used to do. This completed for Adawm and Ḥawwah, one hundred and forty days since their coming out of the garden."],[10,"Then they both stood up that night and prayed to Aluahim. And when it was morning, they went out, and went down westward of the cave, to the place where their corn was, and there rested under the shadow of a tree, as they were accustomed."],[11,"But when there a multitude of beasts came all around them. It was Satan's doing, in his wickedness; in order to wage war against Adawm through marriage."]],"70":[[1,"After this Satan, the hater of all good, took the form of an mal'ak, and with him two others, so that they looked like the three mal'akim who had brought to Adawm gold, incense, and myrrh."],[2,"They passed before Adawm and Ḥawwah while they were under the tree, and greeted Adawm and Ḥawwah with fair words that were full of deceit."],[3,"But when Adawm and Ḥawwah saw their pleasant expression, and heard their sweet speech, Adawm rose, welcomed them, and brought them to Ḥawwah, and they remained all together; Adawm's heart the while, being glad because he thought concerning them, that they were the same mal'akim, who had brought him gold, incense, and myrrh."],[4,"Because, when they came to Adawm the first time, there came over him from them, shalom and joy, through their bringing him good tokens; so Adawm thought that they had come a second time to give him other tokens for him to rejoice therewith. For he did not know it was Satan; therefore he received them with joy and consorted with them."],[5,"Then Satan, the tallest of them, said, \"Rejoice, O Adawm, and be glad. Look, Aluahim has sent us to you to tell you something.\""],[6,"And Adawm said, \"What is it?\" Then Satan answered, \"It is a simple thing, yet it is the Word of Aluahim, will you accept it from us and do it? But if you will not accept it, we will return to Aluahim, and tell Him that you would not receive His Word.\""],[7,"And Satan said again to Adawm, \"Don't be afraid and don't tremble; don't you know us?\""],[8,"But Adawm said, \"I do not know you.\""],[9,"Then Satan said to him, \"I am the mal'ak that brought you gold, and took it to the cave; this other mal'ak is the one that brought you incense; and that third mal'ak, is the one who brought you myrrh when you were on top of the mountain, and who carried you to the cave. 10 But as to the other mal'akim our fellows, who bare you to the cave, Aluahim has not sent them with us this time; for He said to us, 'You will be enough'. \""],[11,"So when Adawm heard these words he believed them, and said to these mal'akim, \"Speak the Word of Aluahim, that I may receive it.\""],[12,"And Satan said to him, \"Swear, and promise me that you will receive it.\""],[13,"Then Adawm said, \"I do not know how to swear and promise.\""],[14,"And Satan said to him, \"Hold out your hand, and put it inside my hand.\""],[15,"Then Adawm held out his hand, and put it into Satan's hand; when Satan said to him, \"Say, now - So true as Aluahim is living, rational, and speaking, who raised the stars in shamayim, and established the dry ground on the waters, and has created me out of the four elements, and out of the dust of the earth - I will not break my promise, nor renounce my word.\""],[16,"And Adawm swore thus."],[17,"Then Satan said to him, \"Look, it is now some time since you came out of the garden, and you know neither wickedness nor evil. But now Aluahim says to you, to take Ḥawwah who came out of your side, and to marry her so that she will bear you children, to comfort you, and to drive from you trouble and sorrow; now this thing is not difficult, neither is there any scandal in it to you. See the previous footnote in Chapter XXXIV regarding the 'four elements'."]],"71":[[1,"But when Adawm heard these words from Satan, he sorrowed much, because of his oath and of his promise, and said, \"Shall I commit adultery with my flesh and my bones, and shall I sin against myself, for Aluahim to destroy me, and to blot me out from off the face of the earth?"],[2,"Since, when at first, I ate of the tree, He drove me out of the garden into this strange land, and deprived me of my bright nature, and brought death over me. If, then, I should do this, He will cut off my life from the earth, and He will cast me into Sheol, and will plague me there a long time. 3 But Aluahim never spoke the words that you have said; and you are not Aluahim's mal'akim, and you weren't sent from Him. But you are devils that have come to me under the false appearance of mal'akim. Away from me; you cursed of Aluahim!\""],[4,"Then those devils fled from before Adawm. And he and Ḥawwah got up, and returned to the Cave of Treasures, and went into it."],[5,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"If you saw what I did, don't tell anyone; for I sinned against Aluahim in swearing by His great name, and I have placed my hand another time into that of Satan.\" Ḥawwah, then, held her shalom, as Adawm told her."],[6,"Then Adawm got up, and spread his hands before Aluahim, beseeching and entreating Him with tears, to forgive him what he had done. And Adawm remained thus standing and praying forty days and forty nights. He neither ate nor drank until he dropped down on the ground from hunger and thirst."],[7,"Then Aluahim sent His Word to Adawm, who raised him up from where he lay, and said to him, \"O Adawm, why have you sworn by My name, and why have you made agreement with Satan another time?\""],[8,"But Adawm cried, and said, \"O Aluahim, forgive me, for I did this unwittingly; believing they were Aluahim's mal'akim.\""],[9,"And Aluahim forgave Adawm, saying to him, \"Beware of Satan.\""],[10,"And He withdrew His Word from Adawm."],[11,"Then Adawm's heart was comforted; and he took Ḥawwah, and they went out of the cave, to prepare some food for their bodies."],[12,"But from that day Adawm struggled in his mind about his marrying Ḥawwah; afraid that if he was to do it, Aluahim would be angry with him."],[13,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah went to the river of water, and sat on the bank, as people do when they enjoy themselves."],[14,"But Satan was jealous of them; and planned to destroy them."]],"72":[[1,"Then Satan, and ten from his hosts, transformed themselves into maidens, unlike any others in the whole world for chen."],[2,"They came up out of the river in presence of Adawm and Ḥawwah, and they said among themselves, \"Come, we will look at the faces of Adawm and Ḥawwah, who are of the men on earth. How beautiful they are, and how different is their look from our own faces.\" Then they came to Adawm and Ḥawwah, and greeted them; and stood wondering at them."],[3,"Adawm and Ḥawwah looked at them also, and wondered at their beauty, and said, \"Is there, then, under us, another world, with such beautiful creatures as these in it?\""],[4,"And those maidens said to Adawm and Ḥawwah, \"Yes, indeed, we are an abundant creation.\""],[5,"Then Adawm said to them, \"But how do you multiply?\""],[6,"And they answered him, \"We have husbands who have married us, and we bear them children, who grow up, and who in their turn marry and are married, and also bear children; and thus we increase. And if so be, O Adawm, you will not believe us, we will show you our husbands and our children.\""],[7,"Then they shouted over the river as if to call their husbands and their children, who came up from the river, men and children; and every man came to his wife, his children being with him."],[8,"But when Adawm and Ḥawwah saw them, they stood dumb, and wondered at them."],[9,"Then they said to Adawm and Ḥawwah, \"See all our husbands and our children? You should marry Ḥawwah, as we have married our husbands, so that you will have children as we have.\" This was a device of Satan to deceive Adawm."],[10,"Satan also thought within himself, \"Aluahim at first commanded Adawm concerning the fruit of the tree, saying to him, 'Eat not of it; else of death you shall die.' But Adawm ate of it, and yet Aluahim did not kill him; He only decreed on him death, and plagues and trials, until the day he shall come out of his body."],[11,"Now, then, if I deceive him to do this thing, and to marry Ḥawwah without Aluahim's permission, Aluahim will kill him then.\""],[12,"Therefore Satan worked this apparition before Adawm and Ḥawwah; because he sought to kill him, and to make him disappear from off the face of the earth."],[13,"Meanwhile the fire of sin came over Adawm, and he thought of committing sin. But he restrained himself, fearing that if he followed this advice of Satan, Aluahim would put him to death."],[14,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah got up, and prayed to Aluahim, while Satan and his hosts went down into the river, in presence of Adawm and Ḥawwah; to let them see that they were going back to their own world."],[15,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah went back to the Cave of Treasures, as they usually did; about evening time."],[16,"And they both got up and prayed to Aluahim that night. Adawm remained standing in prayer, yet not knowing how to pray, by reason of the thoughts in his heart regarding his marrying Ḥawwah; and he continued so until morning."],[17,"And when light came up, Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Get up, let us go below the mountain, where they brought us gold, and let us ask Yahuah concerning this matter.\""],[18,"Then Ḥawwah said, \"What is that matter, O Adawm?\""],[19,"And he answered her, \"That I may request Yahuah to inform me about marrying you; for I will not do it without His permission or else He will make us perish, you and me. For those devils have set my heart on fire, with thoughts of what they showed us, in their sinful apparitions."],[20,"Then Ḥawwah said to Adawm, \"Why need we go below the mountain? Let us rather stand up and pray in our cave to Aluahim, to let us know whether this counsel is good or not.\""],[21,"Then Adawm rose up in prayer and said, \"O Aluahim, you know that we transgressed against you, and from the moment we transgressed, we were stripped of our bright nature; and our body became brutish, requiring food and drink; and with animal desires."],[22,"Command us, O Aluahim, not to give way to them without Your permission, for fear that You will turn us into nothing. Because if you do not give us permission, we shall be overpowered, and follow that advice of Satan; and You will again make us perish."],[23,"If not, then take our nepheshoth from us; let us be rid of this animal lust. And if You give us no order respecting this thing, then sever Ḥawwah from me, and me from her; and place us each far away from the other."],[24,"Then again, O Aluahim, if You separate us from each other, the devils will deceive us with their apparitions that resemble us, and destroy our hearts, and defile our thoughts towards each other. Yet if it is not each of us towards the other, it will, at all events, be through their appearance when the devils come to us in our likeness.\" Here Adawm ended his prayer."]],"73":[[1,"Then Aluahim considered the words of Adawm that they were true, and that he could long await His order, respecting the counsel of Satan."],[2,"And Aluahim approved Adawm in what he had thought concerning this, and in the prayer he had offered in His presence; and the Word of Aluahim came to Adawm and said to him, \"O Adawm, if only you had had this caution at first, before you came out of the garden into this land!\""],[3,"After that, Aluahim sent His mal'ak who had brought gold, and the mal'ak who had brought incense, and the mal'ak who had brought myrrh to Adawm, that they should inform him respecting his marriage to Ḥawwah."],[4,"Then those mal'akim said to Adawm, \"Take the gold and give it to Ḥawwah as a wedding gift, and promise to marry her; then give her some incense and myrrh as a present; and be you, you and she, one flesh.\""],[5,"Adawm obeyed the mal'akim, and took the gold and put it into Ḥawwah's bosom in her garment; and promised to marry her with his hand."],[6,"Then the mal'akim commanded Adawm and Ḥawwah to get up and pray forty days and forty nights; when that was done, then Adawm was to have sexual intercourse with his wife; for then this would be an act pure and undefiled; so that he would have children who would multiply, and replenish the face of the earth."],[7,"Then both Adawm and Ḥawwah received the words of the mal'akim; and the mal'akim departed from them."],[8,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah began to fast and pray, until the end of the forty days; and then they had sexual intercourse, as the mal'akim had told them. And from the time Adawm left the garden until he wedded Ḥawwah, were two hundred and twenty-three days, that is seven months and thirteen days."],[9,"Thus was Satan's war with Adawm defeated."]],"74":[[1,"And they lived on the earth working in order to keep their bodies in good health; and they continued so until the nine months of Ḥawwah's pregnancy were over, and the time drew near when she must give birth."],[2,"Then she said to Adawm, \"The signs placed in this cave since we left the garden indicate that this is a pure place and we will be praying in it again some time. It is not appropriate then, that I should give birth in it. Let us instead go to the sheltering rock cave that was formed by the command of Aluahim when Satan threw a big rock down on us in an attempt to kill us with it."],[3,"Adawm then took Ḥawwah to that cave. When the time came for her to give birth, she strained a lot. Adawm felt sorry, and he was very worried about her because she was close to death and the words of Aluahim to her were being fulfilled: \"In suffering shall you bear a child, and in sorrow shall you bring forth a child.\""],[4,"But when Adawm saw the distress in which Ḥawwah was, he got up and prayed to Aluahim, and said, \"O Yahuah, look at me with the eye of Your mercy, and bring her out of her distress.\""],[5,"And Aluahim looked at His maid-servant Ḥawwah, and delivered her, and she gave birth to her first-born son, and with him a daughter."],[6,"The Adawm rejoiced at Ḥawwah's deliverance, and also over the children she had borne him. And Adawm ministered to Ḥawwah in the cave, until the end of eight days; when they named the son Qayin, and the daughter Luluwa."],[7,"The meaning of Qayin is \"hater,\" because he hated his sister in their mother's womb; before they came out of it. Therefore Adawm named him Qayin."],[8,"But Luluwa means \"beautiful,\" because she was more beautiful than her mother."],[9,"Then Adawm and Ḥawwah waited until Qayin and his sister were forty days old, when Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"We will make an offering and offer it up in behalf of the children.\""],[10,"And Ḥawwah said, \"We will make one offering for the first-born son and then later we shall make one for the daughter.\""]],"75":[[1,"Then Adawm prepared an offering, and he and Ḥawwah offered it up for their children, and brought it to the mizbe'ach they had built at first."],[2,"And Adawm offered up the offering, and asked Aluahim to accept his offering."],[3,"Then Aluahim accepted Adawm's offering, and sent a light from shamayim that shown on the offering. Adawm and his son drew near to the offering, but Ḥawwah and the daughter did not approach it."],[4,"Adawm and his son were joyful as they came down from on the mizbe'ach. Adawm and Ḥawwah waited until the daughter was eighty days old, then Adawm prepared an offering and took it to Ḥawwah and to the children. They went to the mizbe'ach, where Adawm offered it up, as he was accustomed, asking Yahuah to accept his offering."],[5,"And Yahuah accepted the offering of Adawm and Ḥawwah. Then Adawm, Ḥawwah, and the children, drew near together, and came down from the mountain, rejoicing."],[6,"But they returned not to the cave in which they were born; but came to the Cave of Treasures, in order that the children should go around in it, and be baruk with the tokens brought from the garden."],[7,"But after they had been baruk with these tokens, they went back to the cave in which they were born."],[8,"However, before Ḥawwah had offered up the offering, Adawm had taken her, and had gone with her to the river of water, in which they threw themselves at first; and there they washed themselves. Adawm washed his body and Ḥawwah hers also clean, after the suffering and distress that had come over them."],[9,"But Adawm and Ḥawwah, after washing themselves in the river of water, returned every night to the Cave of Treasures, where they prayed and were baruk; and then went back to their cave, where their children were born."],[10,"Adawm and Ḥawwah did this until the children had been weaned. After they were weaned, Adawm made an offering for the nepheshoth of his children in addition to the three times every week he made an offering for them."],[11,"When the children were weaned, Ḥawwah again conceived, and when her pregnancy came to term, she gave birth to another son and daughter. They named the son Heḇal and the daughter Aklia."],[12,"Then at the end of forty days, Adawm made an offering for the son, and at the end of eighty days he made another offering for the daughter, and treated them, as he had previously treated Qayin and his sister Luluwa."],[13,"He brought them to the Cave of Treasures, where they received a berakah, and then returned to the cave where they were born. After these children were born, Ḥawwah stopped having children."]],"76":[[1,"And the children began to grow stronger and taller; but Qayin was hard-hearted, and ruled over his younger brother."],[2,"Often when his father made an offering, Qayin would remain behind and not go with them, to offer up."],[3,"But, as to Heḇal, he had a meek heart, and was obedient to his father and mother. He frequently moved them to make an offering, because he loved it. He prayed and fasted a lot."],[4,"Then came this sign to Heḇal. As he was coming into the Cave of Treasures, and saw the golden rods, the incense and the myrrh, he asked his parents, Adawm and Ḥawwah, to tell him about them and asked, \"Where did you get these from?\""],[5,"Then Adawm told him all that had befallen them. And Heḇal felt deeply about what his father told him."],[6,"Furthermore his father, Adawm, told him of the works of Aluahim, and of the garden. After hearing that, Heḇal remained behind after his father left and stayed the whole of that night in the Cave of Treasures."],[7,"And that night, while he was praying, Satan appeared to him under the figure of a man, who said to him, \"You have frequently moved your father into making offerings, fasting and praying, therefore I will kill you, and make you perish from this world.\""],[8,"But as for Heḇal, he prayed to Aluahim, and drove away Satan from him; and did not believe the words of the devil. Then when it was day, an mal'ak of Aluahim appeared to him, who said to him, \"Do not cut short either fasting, prayer, or offering up an offering to your Aluahim. For, look, Yahuah had accepted your prayer. Be not afraid of the figure which appeared to you in the night, and who cursed you to death.\" And the mal'ak departed from him."],[9,"Then when it was day, Heḇal came to Adawm and Ḥawwah, and told them of the vision he had seen. When they heard it, they grieved much over it, but said nothing to him about it; they only comforted him."],[10,"But as to the hard-hearted Qayin, Satan came to him by night, showed himself and said to him, \"Since Adawm and Ḥawwah love your brother Heḇal so much more than they love you, they wish to join him in marriage to your beautiful sister because they love him. However, they wish to join you in marriage to his ugly sister, because they hate you."],[11,"Now before they do that, I am telling you that you should kill your brother. That way your sister will be left for you, and his sister will be cast away.\""],[12,"And Satan departed from him. But the devil remained behind in Qayin's heart, and frequently aspired to kill his brother."]],"77":[[1,"But when Adawm saw that the older brother hated the younger, he endeavored to soften their hearts, and said to Qayin, \"O my son, take of the fruits of your sowing and make an offering to Aluahim, so that He might forgive you for your wickedness and sin.\""],[2,"He said also to Heḇal, \"Take some of your sowing and make an offering and bring it to Aluahim, so that He might forgive you for your wickedness and sin.\""],[3,"Then Heḇal obeyed his father's voice, took some of his sowing, and made a good offering, and said to his father, Adawm, \"Come with me and show me how to offer it up.\""],[4,"And they went, Adawm and Ḥawwah with him, and they showed him how to offer up his gift on the mizbe'ach. Then after that, they stood up and prayed that Aluahim would accept Heḇal's offering."],[5,"Then Aluahim looked at Heḇal and accepted his offering. And Aluahim was more pleased with Heḇal than with his offering, because of his good heart and pure body. There was no trace of guile in him."],[6,"Then they came down from the mizbe'ach, and went to the cave in which they lived. But Heḇal, by reason of his joy at having made his offering, repeated it three times a week, after the example of his father Adawm."],[7,"But as to Qayin, he did not want to make an offering, but after his father became very angry, he offered up a gift once. He took the smallest of his sheep for an offering and when he offered it up, his eyes were on the lamb."],[8,"Therefore Aluahim did not accept his offering, because his heart was full of murderous thoughts."],[9,"And they all thus lived together in the cave in which Ḥawwah had brought forth, until Qayin was fifteen years old, and Heḇal twelve years old."]],"78":[[1,"Then Adawm said to Ḥawwah, \"Behold the children are grown up; we must think of finding wives for them.\""],[2,"Then Ḥawwah answered, \"How can we do it?\" 3 Then Adawm said to her, \"We will join Heḇal's sister in marriage to Qayin, and Qayin's sister to Heḇal."],[4,"The said Ḥawwah to Adawm, \"I do not like Qayin because he is hard-hearted; but let them stay with us until we offer up to Yahuah in their behalf.\""],[5,"And Adawm said no more."],[6,"Meanwhile Satan came to Qayin in the figure of a man of the field, and said to him, \"Behold Adawm and Ḥawwah have taken counsel together about the marriage of you two; and they have agreed to marry Heḇal's sister to you, and your sister to him."],[7,"But if it was not that I love you, I would not have told you this thing. Yet if you will take my advice, and obey me, I will bring to you on your wedding day beautiful robes, gold and silver in plenty, and my relations will attend you.\""],[8,"Then Qayin said with joy, \"Where are your relations?\""],[9,"And Satan answered, \"My relations are in a garden in the north, where I once meant to bring your father Adawm; but he would not accept my offer."],[10,"But you, if you will receive my words and if you will come to me after your wedding, you shall rest from the misery in which you are; and you shall rest and be better off than your father Adawm.\""],[11,"At these words of Satan Qayin opened his ears, and leaned towards his speech."],[12,"And he did not remain in the field, but he went to Ḥawwah, his mother, and beat her, and cursed her, and said to her, \"Why are you planning to take my sister to wed her to my brother? Am I dead?\""],[13,"His mother, however, quieted him, and sent him to the field where he had been."],[14,"Then when Adawm came, she told him of what Qayin had done."],[15,"But Adawm grieved and held his shalom, and said not a word."],[16,"Then on the next morning Adawm said to Qayin his son, \"Take of your sheep, young and good, and offer them up to your Aluahim; and I will speak to your brother, to make to his Aluahim an offering of corn.\""],[17,"They both obeyed their father Adawm, and they took their offerings, and offered them up on the mountain by the mizbe'ach."],[18,"But Qayin behaved haughtily towards his brother, and shoved him from the mizbe'ach, and would not let him offer up his gift on the mizbe'ach; but he offered his own on it, with a proud heart, full of guile, and fraud."],[19,"But as for Heḇal, he set up stones that were near at hand, and on that, he offered up his gift with a heart humble and free from guile."],[20,"Qayin was then standing by the mizbe'ach on which he had offered up his gift; and he cried to Aluahim to accept his offering; but Aluahim did not accept it from him; neither did a Mighty-like fire come down to consume his offering."],[21,"But he remained standing over against the mizbe'ach, out of humor and meanness, looking towards his brother Heḇal, to see if Aluahim would accept his offering or not."],[22,"And Heḇal prayed to Aluahim to accept his offering. Then a Mighty-like fire came down and consumed his offering. And Aluahim smelled the sweet savor of his offering; because Heḇal loved Him and rejoice in Him."],[23,"And because Aluahim was well pleased with him, He sent him an mal'ak of light in the figure of a man who had partaken of his offering, because He had smelled the sweet savor of his offering, and they comforted Heḇal and strengthened his heart."],[24,"But Qayin was looking on all that took place at his brother's offering, and was angry because of it."],[25,"Then he opened his mouth and blasphemed Aluahim, because He had not accepted his offering."],[26,"But Aluahim said to Qayin, \"Why do you look sad? Be righteous, that I may accept your offering. Not against Me have you murmured, but against yourself. 27 And Aluahim said this to Qayin in rebuke, and because He abhorred him and his offering."],[28,"And Qayin came down from the mizbe'ach, his color changed and with a sad face, and came to his father and mother and told them all that had befallen him. And Adawm grieved much because Aluahim had not accepted Qayin's offering."],[29,"But Heḇal came down rejoicing, and with a gladsome heart, and told his father and mother how Aluahim had accepted his offering. And they rejoiced at it and kissed his face."],[30,"And Heḇal said to his father, \"Because Qayin shoved me from the mizbe'ach, and would not allow me to offer my gift on it, I made an mizbe'ach for myself and offered my gift on it.\""],[31,"But when Adawm heard this he was very sorry, because it was the mizbe'ach he had built at first, and on which he had offered his own gifts."],[32,"As to Qayin, he was so resentful and so angry that he went into the field, where Satan came to him and said to him, \"Since your brother Heḇal has taken refuge with your father Adawm, because you shoved him from the mizbe'ach, they have kissed his face, and they rejoice over him, far more than over you.\""],[33,"When Qayin heard these words of Satan, he was filled with rage; and he let no one know. But he was laying wait to kill his brother, until he brought him into the cave, and then said to him: -"],[34,"\"O brother, the country is so beautiful, and there are such beautiful and pleasurable trees in it, and charming to look at! But brother, you have never been one day in the field to take your pleasure in that place."],[35,"Today, O, my brother, I very much wish you would come with me into the field, to enjoy yourself and to bless our fields and our flocks, for you are righteous, and I love you much, O my brother! But you have alienated yourself from me.\""],[36,"Then Heḇal consented to go with his brother Qayin into the field."],[37,"But before going out, Qayin said to Heḇal, \"Wait for me, until I fetch a staff, because of wild beasts.\""],[38,"Then Heḇal stood waiting in his innocence. But Qayin, the forward, fetched a staff and went out. 39 And they began, Qayin and his brother Heḇal, to walk in the way; Qayin talking to him, and comforting him, to make him forget everything."]],"79":[[1,"And so they went on, until they came to a lonely place, where there were no sheep; then Heḇal said to Qayin, \"Behold, my brother, we are tired from walking; for we see none of the trees, nor of the fruits, nor of the flourishing green plants, nor of the sheep, nor any one of the things of which you told me. Where are those sheep of thine you told me to bless?\""],[2,"Then Qayin said to him, \"Come on, and you shall see many beautiful things very soon, but go before me, until I catch up to you.\""],[3,"Then went Heḇal forward, but Qayin remained behind him."],[4,"And Heḇal was walking in his innocence, without guile; not believing his brother would kill him."],[5,"Then Qayin, when he came up to him, comforted him with his talk, walking a little behind him; then he ran up to him and beat him with the staff, blow after blow, until he was stunned."],[6,"But when Heḇal fell down on the ground, seeing that his brother meant to kill him, he said to Qayin, \"O, my brother, have pity on me. By the breasts we have sucked, don't hit me! By the womb that bore us and that brought us into the world, don't beat me to death with that staff! If you will kill me, take one of these large stones and kill me outright.\""],[7,"Then Qayin, the hard-hearted, and cruel murderer, took a large stone, and beat his brother's head with it, until his brains oozed out, and he wallowed in his blood, before him."],[8,"And Qayin repented not of what he had done."],[9,"But the earth, when the blood of righteous Heḇal fell on it, trembled, as it drank his blood, and would have destroyed Qayin because of it."],[10,"And the blood of Heḇal cried mysteriously to Aluahim, to avenge him of his murderer."],[11,"Then Qayin began at once to dig the ground wherein to lay his brother; for he was trembling from the fear that came over him, when he saw the earth tremble on his account."],[12,"He then cast his brother into the pit he made, and covered him with dust. But the ground would not receive him; but it threw him up at once."],[13,"Again Qayin dug the ground and hid his brother in it; but again the ground threw him up on itself; until three times the ground thus threw up on itself the body of Heḇal."],[14,"The muddy ground threw him up the first time, because he was not the first creation; and it threw him up the second time and would not receive him, because he was righteous and good, and was killed without a cause; and the ground threw him up the third time and would not receive him, that there might remain before his brother a witness against him."],[15,"And so the earth mocked Qayin, until the Word of Aluahim, came to him concerning his brother."],[16,"Then was Aluahim angry, and much displeased at Heḇal's death; and He thundered from shamayim, and lightnings went before Him, and the Word of Yahuah Aluahim came from shamayim to Qayin, and said to him, \"Where is Heḇal your brother?\""],[17,"Then Qayin answered with a proud heart and a gruff voice, \"How, O Aluahim? Am I my brother's keeper?\""],[18,"Then Aluahim said to Qayin, \"Cursed be the earth that has drunk the blood of Heḇal your brother; and as for you, you will always be trembling and shaking; and this will be a mark on you so that whoever finds you, will kill you.\""],[19,"But Qayin cried because Aluahim had said those words to him; and Qayin said to Him, \"O Aluahim, whosoever finds me shall kill me, and I shall be blotted out from the face of the earth.\""],[20,"Then Aluahim said to Qayin, \"Whoever finds you will not kill you;\" because before this, Aluahim had been saying to Qayin, \"I shall put seven punishments on anyone that kills Qayin.\" For as to the word of Aluahim to Qayin, \"Where is your brother?\" Aluahim said it in mercy for him, to try and make him repent."],[21,"For if Qayin had repented at that time, and had said, \"O Aluahim, forgive me my sin, and the murder of my brother,\" Aluahim would then have forgiven him his sin."],[22,"And as to Aluahim saying to Qayin, \"Cursed be the ground that has drunk the blood of your brother\" That also, was Aluahim's mercy on Qayin. For Aluahim did not curse him, but He cursed the ground; although it was not the ground that had killed Heḇal, and committed a wicked sin."],[23,"For it was fitting that the curse should fall on the murderer; yet in mercy did Aluahim so manage His thoughts as that no one should know it, and turn away from Qayin."],[24,"And He said to him, \"Where is your brother?\" To which he answered and said, \"I know not.\" Then the Creator said to him, \"Be trembling and quaking.\""],[25,"Then Qayin trembled and became terrified; and through this sign did Aluahim make him an example before all the creation, as the murderer of his brother. Also did Aluahim bring trembling and terror over him, that he might see the shalom in which he was at first, and see also the trembling and terror he endured at the last; so that he might humble himself before Aluahim, and repent of his sin, and seek the shalom that he enjoyed at first."],[26,"And in the word of Aluahim that said, \"I will put seven punishments on anyone who kills Qayin,\" Aluahim was not seeking to kill Qayin with the sword, but He sought to make him die of fasting, and praying and crying by hard rule, until the time that he was delivered from his sin."],[27,"And the seven punishments are the seven generations during which Aluahim awaited Qayin for the murder of his brother."],[28,"But as to Qayin, ever since he had killed his brother, he could find no rest in any place; but went back to Adawm and Ḥawwah, trembling, terrified, and defiled with blood. . . . End of"]]}});
